-- State Pension Regulations 2015 (S.I. 2015/173), revised text at 2026-04-06
-- (a converter rendering, not the official text) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person who is, or will become, entitled to the State Pension, asking what
-- these Regulations mean for when and how their State Pension is claimed, paid and
-- affected by their choices.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the layer-1 modules imported above as
-- the questions that person would ask. Nothing here is new law, and no layer-1 module
-- changes to suit it. Every question takes plain inputs (yes/no, numbers, dates, and the
-- modules' own lists of choices), one for each fact the person can state, each with an
-- @desc worded as the person would be asked. The records the rules expect are built in
-- each question's WHERE from those answers, and the SAME module rule is then called.
-- A record field that the rule called never reads is given a fixed placeholder, with a
-- comment saying so.
--
-- ASSUMPTIONS THE SEAT MAKES (also in NOTES.md):
--   * Every answer assumes the first question below, "Do these Regulations apply to me?",
--     is answered yes (reg 1(3)). The questions do not each re-ask it.
--   * Pensionable age is fixed by Acts that are not among the inputs, so the date the
--     person reaches it is asked, not worked out.
--   * A judgment the Regulations leave to the Secretary of State or another official is
--     asked as a fact ("Does the Secretary of State consider it reasonable ...?"), so the
--     answer is conditional on it.
--   * The person asking is alive (reg 6(2)(a)): that field is fixed, not asked.
--   * A list the rules take (change dates, parts of a deferral, benefits received) is asked
--     one item at a time where one item decides the answer; NOTES.md records where it does
--     not.

§ `State Pension Regulations 2015 -- the questions of a person who is or will be entitled to the State Pension`

-- Regulation 1: scope. Every answer below assumes the first question here is answered yes
-- (a person who reaches pensionable age before 6 April 2016 is outside the Regulations,
-- except Part 5; see NOTES.md, forks F8 and finding 1).
§§ `Do these Regulations apply to me?`

-- Reg 1(3). The Regulations (except Part 5, which applies to everyone) do not apply to a person who
-- reaches pensionable age before 6 April 2016.
@export Do these Regulations apply to me (reg 1(3))?
GIVEN `the date I reach pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you reach, or did you reach, State Pension age?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do these Regulations apply to me` IF
    `regulation 1(3): these Regulations (except Part 5) apply to the person` `the date I reach pensionable age`

-- Reg 1(4). Graduated retirement benefit means a benefit under section 36 or section 37 of the National
-- Insurance Act 1965.
@export Does the benefit I get count as graduated retirement benefit (reg 1(4))?
GIVEN `the benefit I get` IS A BenefitUnder1965Act @desc Which provision of the National Insurance Act 1965 is the benefit paid under?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the benefit I get count as graduated retirement benefit` IF
    `regulation 1(4): the benefit is graduated retirement benefit` `the benefit I get`

-- Reg 1(5). If either of two people is married to a third person at the time in question, the two are
-- treated as not married to each other then. The paragraph speaks of marriage only (fork F9).
@export Are my spouse or civil partner and I treated as married or civil partners at that time (reg 1(5))?
GIVEN `how my spouse or civil partner and I were related` IS A KindOfRelationship @desc Were you and the other person married to each other, or civil partners of each other?
      `either of us was married to someone else at the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At that time, was either of you married to a third person?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my spouse or civil partner and I treated as married or civil partners at that time` IF
    `regulation 1(5): the two people are treated as spouses or civil partners at the time` `how my spouse or civil partner and I were related` `either of us was married to someone else at the time`

-- Reg 1A. The full rate for section 3(1) of the Pensions Act 2014 is 241.30 pounds a week (the figure in the
-- 2026-04-06 text; it takes no input and does not say from when it applies, fork F10).
@export What is the full weekly rate of the State Pension, in pounds (reg 1A)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the full weekly rate of the State Pension, in pounds` IS
    `regulation 1A: the full rate of the state pension, in pounds per week`


-- Regulations 2 and 3. A situation: ask "Are you, or have you been, in prison, in custody or on remand?"
-- before showing this group.
§§ `If I am in prison or on remand`

-- Regs 2 and 3. A person is not paid the State Pension for a period in which they are a prisoner of one of the
-- four kinds in reg 2(2), except that a person remanded in custody is paid unless a described sentence is later
-- imposed (reg 3). Reg 2(4) (reg 13 has no effect for relevant benefits) is a gap: see NOTES.md, fork F7.
@export Is my State Pension withheld for a day on which I am in prison or in custody (regs 2, 3)?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
      `I am in Great Britain on that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On that day, are you in Great Britain?
      `I am imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with criminal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On that day, are you imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings?
      `I am a prisoner who is unlawfully at large` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On that day, are you a prisoner who is unlawfully at large?
      `I am detained under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On that day, are you detained under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983 (removal to hospital of people serving prison sentences)?
      `the Secretary of State has certified a release date for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State certified a release date for you under section 50(3) of that Act?
      `the release date the Secretary of State certified` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is that date? (Give any date if there is none.)
      `I am detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On that day, are you detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003 (transfer of prisoners for treatment)?
      `in similar circumstances in Great Britain I would not have been a prisoner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are outside Great Britain: in similar circumstances in Great Britain, would you not have been a prisoner?
      `I am remanded in custody for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you remanded in custody for an offence?
      `a sentence has since been imposed for that offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a sentence since been imposed on you for that offence?
      `the kind of sentence imposed` IS A KindOfSentence @desc What kind of sentence was imposed? (Choose any other sentence if none was.)
      `that sentence was imposed outside Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that sentence imposed outside Great Britain?
      `in similar circumstances in Great Britain such a sentence would not have been imposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was imposed outside Great Britain: in similar circumstances in Great Britain, would such a sentence not have been imposed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my State Pension withheld for a day on which I am in prison or in custody` IF
    `regulation 2(1): the state pension is not to be paid for the day` `the day I am asking about` `my status`
    WHERE
        `my custody` MEANS Custody WITH
            `the person is in Great Britain` IS `I am in Great Britain on that day`
            `the person is imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings` IS `I am imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with criminal proceedings`
            `the person is a prisoner who is unlawfully at large` IS `I am a prisoner who is unlawfully at large`
            `the person is detained under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983` IS `I am detained under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983`
            `the release date that the Secretary of State has certified, if any` IS IF `the Secretary of State has certified a release date for me` THEN JUST `the release date the Secretary of State certified` ELSE NOTHING
            `the person is detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003` IS `I am detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003`
            `in similar circumstances in Great Britain the person would not have been a prisoner` IS `in similar circumstances in Great Britain I would not have been a prisoner`
        `my sentence` MEANS Sentence WITH
            `the kind of sentence` IS `the kind of sentence imposed`
            `the sentence was imposed outside Great Britain` IS `that sentence was imposed outside Great Britain`
            `in similar circumstances in Great Britain a sentence of imprisonment or detention would not have been imposed` IS `in similar circumstances in Great Britain such a sentence would not have been imposed`
        `my status` MEANS PrisonStatus WITH
            `the person's custody on the day` IS `my custody`
            `the person is remanded in custody for an offence` IS `I am remanded in custody for an offence`
            `a sentence later imposed for the offence, if any` IS IF `a sentence has since been imposed for that offence` THEN JUST `my sentence` ELSE NOTHING


-- Regulations 4 to 6. A situation: ask "Did your late spouse or civil partner defer their State Pension, so that you
-- can choose between a lump sum and a survivor's pension?" before showing this group.
§§ `If my late spouse or civil partner deferred their State Pension: my choice of a lump sum or a pension (regs 4 to 6)`

-- Reg 4(1) to (3). The period is three months starting on the date in the most recent notice confirming the
-- choice; if the person chooses before any notice, it runs from the later of their claim and their spouse's
-- or civil partner's death to the day they choose.
@export Is my choice between a lump sum and a survivor's pension made in time (reg 4)?
GIVEN `section 8(1) of the Pensions Act 2014 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 8(1) of the Pensions Act 2014 apply to you (your late spouse or civil partner deferred their State Pension and you may choose between a lump sum and a survivor's pension)?
      `I was sent a notice confirming that I may make the choice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Secretary of State send you a notice confirming that you may make the choice?
      `the date in the most recent such notice` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the date in the most recent such notice? (Give any date if you got none.)
      `the date I claimed my State Pension` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you claim your State Pension?
      `the date my spouse or civil partner died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your spouse or civil partner die?
      `the date I make my choice` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you make (or did you make) your choice?
GIVETH A ChoiceTiming
DECIDE `Is my choice between a lump sum and a survivor's pension made in time` IS
    `regulation 4: whether the choice is made within the period` `my choice facts`
    WHERE
        `my choice facts` MEANS ChoicePeriodFacts WITH
            `the person falls within section 8(1) of the 2014 Act` IS `section 8(1) of the Pensions Act 2014 applies to me`
            `the date in the most recent notice, issued before the choice was made, confirming that the person may make the choice, if any` IS IF `I was sent a notice confirming that I may make the choice` THEN JUST `the date in the most recent such notice` ELSE NOTHING
            `the date the person claims a state pension` IS `the date I claimed my State Pension`
            `the date the person's spouse or civil partner died` IS `the date my spouse or civil partner died`
            `the date the person makes the choice` IS `the date I make my choice`

-- Reg 4(4). A late choice is allowed where the Secretary of State considers it reasonable in the particular case
-- and any lump sum already paid has been repaid in full, in the currency it was paid in. The reasonableness
-- judgment is the Secretary of State's, so it is taken as an input (the rule answers conditionally).
@export May I still make a late choice between a lump sum and a survivor's pension (reg 4(4))?
GIVEN `the Secretary of State considers it reasonable to let me choose late` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Secretary of State consider it reasonable, in your case, to let you choose late?
      `an amount has been paid to me as, or on account of, a lump sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has any amount been paid to you as, or on account of, a lump sum?
      `I have repaid that amount to the Secretary of State in full` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you repaid that amount to the Secretary of State in full?
      `I repaid it in the currency in which it was paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you repay it in the currency in which it was originally paid?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I still make a late choice between a lump sum and a survivor's pension` IF
    `regulation 4(4): a late choice may be made` `my late choice facts`
    WHERE
        `my late choice facts` MEANS LateChoiceFacts WITH
            `the Secretary of State considers it reasonable in the particular case` IS `the Secretary of State considers it reasonable to let me choose late`
            `an amount has been paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum under section 8(4) of the 2014 Act` IS `an amount has been paid to me as, or on account of, a lump sum`
            `that amount has been repaid to the Secretary of State in full` IS `I have repaid that amount to the Secretary of State in full`
            `that amount has been repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid` IS `I repaid it in the currency in which it was paid`

-- Reg 4(5). The lump sum is reduced to nil where the person makes a late choice to be paid a state pension.
@export How much lump sum am I paid if I make a late choice of a survivor's pension, in pounds (reg 4(5))?
GIVEN `the lump sum I would otherwise be paid` IS A NUMBER @desc What lump sum, in pounds, would you otherwise be paid?
      `I make a late choice to be paid a survivor's pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you making a late choice to be paid a survivor's pension instead?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much lump sum am I paid if I make a late choice of a survivor's pension, in pounds` IS
    `regulation 4(5): the amount of the lump sum` `the lump sum I would otherwise be paid` `I make a late choice to be paid a survivor's pension`

-- Reg 5. The choice is made in writing to an office, or by telephone to a number, that the Secretary of State has
-- specified to the person in writing; where the Secretary of State directs that writing must be used, only writing
-- will do. NOTHING where section 8(1) does not apply to the person.
@export Do I make my choice in the manner the Regulations require (reg 5)?
GIVEN `section 8(1) of the Pensions Act 2014 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 8(1) of the Pensions Act 2014 apply to you (you may choose between a lump sum and a survivor's pension)?
      `the way I make my choice` IS A MannerOfNotice @desc How do you make your choice: in writing to an office the Secretary of State specified to you, by telephone to a number the Secretary of State specified to you, or in another way?
      `the Secretary of State has directed that I must use writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State directed that you must use writing to an office?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I make my choice in the manner the Regulations require` IS
    `regulation 5: the choice is made in the manner required` `section 8(1) of the Pensions Act 2014 applies to me` `the way I make my choice` `the Secretary of State has directed that I must use writing`

-- Reg 6(1), (2); reg 18(7) applies the same conditions to a choice under reg 18. All of (a) to (h) must hold.
-- The person asking is alive (reg 6(2)(a)): the field is fixed, not asked.
@export May I change my choice of a lump sum or a survivor's pension (regs 6(1), 18(7))?
GIVEN `I have applied to change my choice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied to change your choice?
      `the date of my application` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you apply (or will you apply) to change it?
      `the date in the notification confirming my choice` IS A DATE @desc What date is in the notification the Secretary of State sent to confirm your choice?
      `the Secretary of State has allowed me a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State allowed you a longer period than three months to apply?
      `the last day of that longer period` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the last day of that period? (Give any date if there is none.)
      `the way I apply` IS A MannerOfNotice @desc How do you apply: in writing to an office the Secretary of State specified to you, by telephone to a number the Secretary of State specified to you, or in another way?
      `the Secretary of State has directed that I must use writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State directed that you must use writing to an office?
      `the choice I ask to change to` IS A PaymentChoice @desc Which do you ask to change to: a lump sum, or a state pension?
      `an amount has been paid to me as, or on account of, a lump sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has any amount been paid to you as, or on account of, a lump sum?
      `I have repaid that amount to the Secretary of State in full` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you repaid that amount to the Secretary of State in full?
      `the date I finished repaying it` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you finish repaying it? (Give any date if you have not.)
      `I repaid it in the currency in which it was paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you repay it in the currency in which it was originally paid?
      `the amount of the state pension that would be paid to me` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount, in pounds, would be paid to you by way of the state pension?
      `the amount of the lump sum that would be paid to me` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount, in pounds, would be paid to you as the lump sum?
      `I have already changed my choice once for this deferral` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you already changed your choice once in respect of this deferral?
      `my choice was treated as made after a death under the Claims and Payments Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your choice treated as made under regulation 30(5G) or (5H) of the Social Security (Claims and Payments) Regulations 1987 (payments on death)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I change my choice of a lump sum or a survivor's pension` IF
    `regulation 6(1): the choice may be altered` `my alteration`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholder: the person asking is alive (reg 6(2)(a) reads this field; NOTES.md, seat assumptions).
        `my alteration` MEANS AlterationFacts WITH
            `the person who made the choice has since died` IS FALSE
            `an application is made to alter the choice` IS `I have applied to change my choice`
            `the date of the application` IS `the date of my application`
            `the date in the notification issued by the Secretary of State confirming the choice` IS `the date in the notification confirming my choice`
            `the last day of any longer period that the Secretary of State considers reasonable` IS IF `the Secretary of State has allowed me a longer period` THEN JUST `the last day of that longer period` ELSE NOTHING
            `the manner of the application` IS `the way I apply`
            `the Secretary of State directs that writing to an office must be used in this case` IS `the Secretary of State has directed that I must use writing`
            `the choice the application asks for` IS `the choice I ask to change to`
            `an amount has been paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum under section 8 of the 2014 Act` IS `an amount has been paid to me as, or on account of, a lump sum`
            `that amount has been repaid to the Secretary of State in full` IS `I have repaid that amount to the Secretary of State in full`
            `the date on which the repayment in full was completed` IS `the date I finished repaying it`
            `that amount was repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid` IS `I repaid it in the currency in which it was paid`
            `the amount that would be paid by way of a state pension under section 9 of the 2014 Act` IS `the amount of the state pension that would be paid to me`
            `the amount that would be paid as a lump sum under section 8 of the 2014 Act` IS `the amount of the lump sum that would be paid to me`
            `a previous alteration has been made in respect of the same deferral` IS `I have already changed my choice once for this deferral`
            `the choice has been treated as made under regulation 30(5G) or (5H) of the Claims and Payments Regulations 1987` IS `my choice was treated as made after a death under the Claims and Payments Regulations`

-- Reg 6(2)(c). Three months starting on the date in the notification, or such longer period as the Secretary
-- of State considers reasonable (the later end is taken).
@export By when must I apply to change my choice (reg 6(2)(c))?
GIVEN `the date in the notification confirming my choice` IS A DATE @desc What date is in the notification the Secretary of State sent to confirm your choice?
      `the Secretary of State has allowed me a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State allowed you a longer period than three months to apply?
      `the last day of that longer period` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the last day of that period? (Give any date if there is none.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I apply to change my choice` IS
    `regulation 6(2)(c): the last day of the period within which the application must be made` `my alteration`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholders: the rule reads only the notification date and the longer period.
        `my alteration` MEANS AlterationFacts WITH
            `the person who made the choice has since died` IS FALSE
            `an application is made to alter the choice` IS TRUE
            `the date of the application` IS `the date in the notification confirming my choice`
            `the date in the notification issued by the Secretary of State confirming the choice` IS `the date in the notification confirming my choice`
            `the last day of any longer period that the Secretary of State considers reasonable` IS IF `the Secretary of State has allowed me a longer period` THEN JUST `the last day of that longer period` ELSE NOTHING
            `the manner of the application` IS `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State`
            `the Secretary of State directs that writing to an office must be used in this case` IS FALSE
            `the choice the application asks for` IS `a state pension`
            `an amount has been paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum under section 8 of the 2014 Act` IS FALSE
            `that amount has been repaid to the Secretary of State in full` IS FALSE
            `the date on which the repayment in full was completed` IS `the date in the notification confirming my choice`
            `that amount was repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid` IS FALSE
            `the amount that would be paid by way of a state pension under section 9 of the 2014 Act` IS 0
            `the amount that would be paid as a lump sum under section 8 of the 2014 Act` IS 0
            `a previous alteration has been made in respect of the same deferral` IS FALSE
            `the choice has been treated as made under regulation 30(5G) or (5H) of the Claims and Payments Regulations 1987` IS FALSE

-- Reg 6(2)(e). The person's duty: a lump sum already paid must be repaid in full, in the currency it was paid in,
-- within the application period, before the choice can become a state pension. Nothing to repay if none was paid.
@export Have I repaid my lump sum as the Regulations require before I change to a survivor's pension (reg 6(2)(e))?
GIVEN `the choice I ask to change to` IS A PaymentChoice @desc Which do you ask to change to: a lump sum, or a state pension?
      `an amount has been paid to me as, or on account of, a lump sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has any amount been paid to you as, or on account of, a lump sum?
      `I have repaid that amount to the Secretary of State in full` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you repaid that amount to the Secretary of State in full?
      `the date I finished repaying it` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you finish repaying it? (Give any date if you have not.)
      `I repaid it in the currency in which it was paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you repay it in the currency in which it was originally paid?
      `the date in the notification confirming my choice` IS A DATE @desc What date is in the notification the Secretary of State sent to confirm your choice?
      `the Secretary of State has allowed me a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State allowed you a longer period than three months to apply?
      `the last day of that longer period` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the last day of that period? (Give any date if there is none.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I repaid my lump sum as the Regulations require before I change to a survivor's pension` IF
    `regulation 6(2)(e): where the alteration is to a state pension, any lump sum has been repaid` `my alteration`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholders: the rule reads the new choice, the lump sum facts, and (through the period) the notification date and longer period.
        `my alteration` MEANS AlterationFacts WITH
            `the person who made the choice has since died` IS FALSE
            `an application is made to alter the choice` IS TRUE
            `the date of the application` IS `the date in the notification confirming my choice`
            `the date in the notification issued by the Secretary of State confirming the choice` IS `the date in the notification confirming my choice`
            `the last day of any longer period that the Secretary of State considers reasonable` IS IF `the Secretary of State has allowed me a longer period` THEN JUST `the last day of that longer period` ELSE NOTHING
            `the manner of the application` IS `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State`
            `the Secretary of State directs that writing to an office must be used in this case` IS FALSE
            `the choice the application asks for` IS `the choice I ask to change to`
            `an amount has been paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum under section 8 of the 2014 Act` IS `an amount has been paid to me as, or on account of, a lump sum`
            `that amount has been repaid to the Secretary of State in full` IS `I have repaid that amount to the Secretary of State in full`
            `the date on which the repayment in full was completed` IS `the date I finished repaying it`
            `that amount was repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid` IS `I repaid it in the currency in which it was paid`
            `the amount that would be paid by way of a state pension under section 9 of the 2014 Act` IS 0
            `the amount that would be paid as a lump sum under section 8 of the 2014 Act` IS 0
            `a previous alteration has been made in respect of the same deferral` IS FALSE
            `the choice has been treated as made under regulation 30(5G) or (5H) of the Claims and Payments Regulations 1987` IS FALSE

-- Reg 6(3). Where the person changes to a lump sum because the pension paid is less than the lump sum, the pension
-- already paid counts as paid on account of the lump sum.
@export Is the State Pension I have been paid treated as paid on account of my lump sum (reg 6(3))?
GIVEN `the choice I ask to change to` IS A PaymentChoice @desc Which do you ask to change to: a lump sum, or a state pension?
      `the amount of the state pension that would be paid to me` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount, in pounds, would be paid to you by way of the state pension?
      `the amount of the lump sum that would be paid to me` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount, in pounds, would be paid to you as the lump sum?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the State Pension I have been paid treated as paid on account of my lump sum` IF
    `regulation 6(3): the state pension already paid is treated as paid on account of the lump sum` `my alteration`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholders: the rule reads only the new choice and the two amounts.
        `my alteration` MEANS AlterationFacts WITH
            `the person who made the choice has since died` IS FALSE
            `an application is made to alter the choice` IS TRUE
            `the date of the application` IS (YMD 2027 3 1)
            `the date in the notification issued by the Secretary of State confirming the choice` IS (YMD 2027 1 15)
            `the last day of any longer period that the Secretary of State considers reasonable` IS NOTHING
            `the manner of the application` IS `in writing to an office specified in writing by the Secretary of State`
            `the Secretary of State directs that writing to an office must be used in this case` IS FALSE
            `the choice the application asks for` IS `the choice I ask to change to`
            `an amount has been paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum under section 8 of the 2014 Act` IS FALSE
            `that amount has been repaid to the Secretary of State in full` IS FALSE
            `the date on which the repayment in full was completed` IS (YMD 2027 2 20)
            `that amount was repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid` IS FALSE
            `the amount that would be paid by way of a state pension under section 9 of the 2014 Act` IS `the amount of the state pension that would be paid to me`
            `the amount that would be paid as a lump sum under section 8 of the 2014 Act` IS `the amount of the lump sum that would be paid to me`
            `a previous alteration has been made in respect of the same deferral` IS FALSE
            `the choice has been treated as made under regulation 30(5G) or (5H) of the Claims and Payments Regulations 1987` IS FALSE


-- Regulations 7 to 12A. A situation: ask "Have you deferred, or are you thinking of deferring, your own State Pension?"
-- before showing this group.
§§ `If I put off claiming my own State Pension (regs 7 to 12A)`

-- Reg 7. A person who has become entitled to a state pension may opt to suspend it by giving notice to the Secretary of State,
-- in writing to a specified office or by telephone to a specified number, or in writing only where the Secretary of State directs.
@export Have I validly opted to suspend my State Pension (reg 7)?
GIVEN `I have become entitled to a State Pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you become entitled to a State Pension under Part 1 of the Pensions Act 2014?
      `I have given notice to the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given notice to the Secretary of State that you want to suspend it?
      `the way I gave notice` IS A MannerOfNotice @desc How did you give notice: in writing to an office the Secretary of State specified to you, by telephone to a number the Secretary of State specified to you, or in another way?
      `the Secretary of State has directed that I must use writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State directed that you must use writing to an office?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I validly opted to suspend my State Pension` IF
    `regulation 7: the person has opted to suspend their entitlement` `I have become entitled to a State Pension` `I have given notice to the Secretary of State` `the way I gave notice` `the Secretary of State has directed that I must use writing`

-- Reg 8(2). Any date not before the day the option was exercised and not after 28 days starting with that day
-- (the latest is therefore the exercise day plus 27, fork F13).
@export Is the date I picked for my suspension to start one the Regulations allow (reg 8(2))?
GIVEN `the date I exercised my option` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you exercise your option to suspend?
      `the date I picked for the suspension to start` IS A DATE @desc What date do you pick for the suspension to start?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the date I picked for my suspension to start one the Regulations allow` IF
    `regulation 8(2): the specified date is one the Regulations allow` `the date I exercised my option` `the date I picked for the suspension to start`

-- Reg 8. The date the person specifies if it is allowed, otherwise the day the option was exercised.
@export From what date does my suspension take effect (reg 8)?
GIVEN `the date I exercised my option` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you exercise your option to suspend?
      `I picked a date for the suspension to start` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you pick a date for the suspension to start?
      `the date I picked for the suspension to start` IS A DATE @desc If so, what date? (Give any date if you did not.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From what date does my suspension take effect` IS
    `regulation 8: the date from which the suspension takes effect` `the date I exercised my option` (IF `I picked a date for the suspension to start` THEN JUST `the date I picked for the suspension to start` ELSE NOTHING)

-- Reg 9. The person may cancel the suspension for the whole or part of a past period of up to 12 months before the day
-- they cancel, by claiming their State Pension while it is suspended.
@export Can I cancel my suspension for this past period (reg 9)?
GIVEN `I have opted to suspend my State Pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you opted to suspend your State Pension?
      `I claim my State Pension while it is suspended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you claiming your State Pension while it is suspended?
      `the date of my claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you make that claim?
      `the first day of the period I want to cancel` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the period you want the suspension cancelled for?
      `the last day of the period I want to cancel` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of that period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I cancel my suspension for this past period` IF
    `regulation 9: the suspension can be cancelled for the period` `I have opted to suspend my State Pension` `I claim my State Pension while it is suspended` `the date of my claim` `the first day of the period I want to cancel` `the last day of the period I want to cancel`

-- Reg 9(3). Up to 12 months before the day the person cancels the suspension.
@export How far back can I cancel my suspension (reg 9(3))?
GIVEN `the date I cancel the suspension` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you cancel the suspension (by claiming your State Pension)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `How far back can I cancel my suspension` IS
    `regulation 9(3): the earliest day to which a cancellation can reach back` `the date I cancel the suspension`

-- Reg 11. A day does not count if the person received one of the listed benefits that day, or if their spouse, civil partner or
-- housemate received an increase of one in respect of them, or if they would not have been paid because they were a prisoner.
-- Only 'any' matters, so one benefit is asked about, not a list.
@export Is this day left out of the days counted towards my deferral (reg 11)?
GIVEN `I received one of the listed benefits on that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On that day, did you receive any of these benefits: state pension credit, income support, income-related employment and support allowance, income-based jobseeker's allowance, universal credit, carer's allowance, carer support payment, unemployability supplement, severe disablement allowance, widow's pension, widowed mother's allowance or incapacity benefit?
      `the listed benefit I received` IS A ListedBenefit @desc Which one? (Choose any if you received none.)
      `someone received an increase of one of the listed benefits for me on that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On that day, did another person receive an increase of one of those benefits in respect of you?
      `the listed benefit they received an increase of` IS A ListedBenefit @desc Which one? (Choose any if none.)
      `that person is married to me, in a civil partnership with me, or lives with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that person married to you, in a civil partnership with you, or living with you?
      `I would not have been paid on that day because I was a prisoner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you not have been paid the State Pension on that day, had it not been deferred, because you were a prisoner?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this day left out of the days counted towards my deferral` IF
    `regulation 11: the day does not count in determining the number of whole weeks` `my day`
    WHERE
        `my day` MEANS DayFacts WITH
            `the listed benefits that the deferred person received on the day` IS IF `I received one of the listed benefits on that day` THEN LIST `the listed benefit I received` ELSE EMPTY
            `the listed benefits of which another person received an increase in respect of the deferred person on the day` IS IF `someone received an increase of one of the listed benefits for me on that day` THEN LIST `the listed benefit they received an increase of` ELSE EMPTY
            `that other person is married to, in a civil partnership with, or residing with the deferred person` IS `that person is married to me, in a civil partnership with me, or lives with me`
            `the deferred person would not, if their entitlement was not deferred, have been paid the state pension on the day because they were a prisoner` IS `I would not have been paid on that day because I was a prisoner`

-- Reg 12. Days left out under reg 11 are taken off the deferral period; a part week left over counts as a whole week
-- (fork F14). NOTHING where more days are left out than the period has.
@export How many whole weeks count towards my deferral (reg 12)?
GIVEN `the first day of my deferral` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of your deferral?
      `the last day of my deferral` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of your deferral?
      `the number of days left out under regulation 11` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of the deferral are left out under regulation 11?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many whole weeks count towards my deferral` IS
    `regulation 12: the number of whole weeks counted` `my deferral` `the number of days left out under regulation 11`
    WHERE
        `my deferral` MEANS DeferralPeriod WITH
            `first day of the deferral` IS `the first day of my deferral`
            `last day of the deferral` IS `the last day of my deferral`

-- Reg 10 with section 17(4) of the 2014 Act (not an input; fork F14): one-ninth of 1% of the weekly rate for each whole week.
@export By how much is my weekly State Pension increased for the weeks I deferred, in pounds (reg 10)?
GIVEN `the whole weeks counted` IS A NUMBER @desc How many whole weeks count towards your deferral?
      `my weekly rate of State Pension without the deferral` IS A NUMBER @desc What weekly rate of State Pension, in pounds, would you have had without the deferral?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `By how much is my weekly State Pension increased for the weeks I deferred, in pounds` IS
    `regulation 10: the weekly increase for the weeks counted` `the whole weeks counted` `my weekly rate of State Pension without the deferral`

-- Reg 12A(1). It applies where, in the deferral period, the weekly rate would have changed other than by up-rating.
-- Only one change date is asked about (a list of dates is not a plain input); NOTES.md records the limit.
@export Does regulation 12A change my increase because my weekly State Pension would have changed during my deferral (reg 12A(1))?
GIVEN `the first day of my deferral` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of your deferral?
      `the last day of my deferral` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of your deferral?
      `my weekly rate would have changed during the deferral other than by up-rating` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During the deferral, would your weekly rate of State Pension have changed for a reason other than an up-rating increase?
      `the date of that change` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (Give any date if no.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does regulation 12A change my increase because my weekly State Pension would have changed during my deferral` IF
    `regulation 12A(1): regulation 12A applies` `my deferral` `my changes`
    WHERE
        `my deferral` MEANS DeferralPeriod WITH
            `first day of the deferral` IS `the first day of my deferral`
            `last day of the deferral` IS `the last day of my deferral`
        `my changes` MEANS IF `my weekly rate would have changed during the deferral other than by up-rating` THEN LIST `the date of that change` ELSE EMPTY

-- Reg 12A(2). For each modification period: one-ninth of 1% of the weekly rate immediately before the end of the period, for each whole week counted in it.
-- How the counted weeks are shared among the periods is not said (fork F16), so the weeks for the period are an input.
@export What is my increment for a period in which my weekly State Pension would not have changed, in pounds (reg 12A(2))?
GIVEN `the whole weeks counted in that period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many whole weeks count in that period?
      `the weekly rate I would have had immediately before the end of that period` IS A NUMBER @desc What weekly rate of State Pension, in pounds, would you have had immediately before the end of that period?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my increment for a period in which my weekly State Pension would not have changed, in pounds` IS
    `regulation 12A(2): the increment for a modification period` `the whole weeks counted in that period` `the weekly rate I would have had immediately before the end of that period`


§§ `Do I have enough qualifying years? (reg 13)`

-- Reg 13. The minimum is ten for the reduced rate and ten for the transitional rate. The Regulations set no number for the full rate.
@export Do I have enough qualifying years for this State Pension (reg 13)?
GIVEN `the kind of State Pension` IS A KindOfStatePension @desc Which State Pension are you asking about: the reduced rate, the transitional rate, or the full rate?
      `the number of qualifying years I have` IS A NUMBER @desc How many qualifying years do you have?
GIVETH A EnoughYears
DECIDE `Do I have enough qualifying years for this State Pension` IS
    `regulation 13: whether the person has the minimum number of qualifying years` `the kind of State Pension` `the number of qualifying years I have`


-- Regulation 14 and the Schedule, which insert regulations 6 and 7 into the Sharing of State Scheme Rights (Provision of Information and Valuation)
-- (No.2) Regulations 2000. A situation: ask "Is a divorce, or the end of a civil partnership, affecting your State Pension rights?"
-- before showing this group.
§§ `If my pension rights are shared on divorce or the end of a civil partnership (regulation 14 and the Schedule)`

-- Inserted reg 6(1). The person with the rights, or the court by order, gets paragraphs (2) to (6); the spouse or civil partner gets paragraph (6) only.
-- What the Secretary of State must furnish is what the person is owed.
@export What information must the Secretary of State give about my pension rights when sharing is considered (inserted reg 6(1))?
GIVEN `who makes the request` IS A WhoRequests @desc Who makes the request: you (the person with the pension rights), the court by an order, or your spouse or civil partner?
GIVETH A InformationToBeFurnished
DECIDE `What information must the Secretary of State give about my pension rights when sharing is considered` IS
    `inserted regulation 6(1): the information the Secretary of State must furnish` `who makes the request`

-- Inserted reg 6(2) to (4). As at the date the request is received, unless a relevant date is given: on or after 6 April 2016 the new state scheme rights as at
-- that date; before it, the previous old scheme rights. NOTHING for a request received before 6 April 2016.
@export Which valuation of my pension rights will I be given (inserted reg 6(2) to (4))?
GIVEN `a relevant date applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a relevant date for the valuation (a date as at which the valuation is wanted)?
      `the relevant date` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is that date? (Give any date if there is none.)
      `the date the Secretary of State receives the request` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the Secretary of State receive the request?
GIVETH A MAYBE ValuationGiven
DECIDE `Which valuation of my pension rights will I be given` IS
    `inserted regulation 6(2) to (4): the valuation to be given` (IF `a relevant date applies` THEN JUST `the relevant date` ELSE NOTHING) `the date the Secretary of State receives the request`

-- Inserted reg 6(5). Where the relevant date is before 6 April 2016 and the request is received on or after it.
@export May I be given the amount of my former Category A retirement pension (inserted reg 6(5))?
GIVEN `a relevant date applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a relevant date for the valuation (a date as at which the valuation is wanted)?
      `the relevant date` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is that date? (Give any date if there is none.)
      `the date the Secretary of State receives the request` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the Secretary of State receive the request?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I be given the amount of my former Category A retirement pension` IF
    `inserted regulation 6(5): the amount of the former Category A entitlement may be given` (IF `a relevant date applies` THEN JUST `the relevant date` ELSE NOTHING) `the date the Secretary of State receives the request`

-- Inserted reg 6(7), (8). Three months from receipt; six weeks if the person has notified that proceedings have begun; a shorter period the court sets (only for a
-- court's order); one month where the spouse asks, or the request is for no valuation or amount. The earliest that applies is the last day (fork F18).
@export By when must the Secretary of State give me the information that has been asked for (inserted reg 6(7), (8))?
GIVEN `who makes the request` IS A WhoRequests @desc Who makes the request: you (the person with the pension rights), the court by an order, or your spouse or civil partner?
      `the date the Secretary of State receives the request or order` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the Secretary of State receive the request or order?
      `the request or order asks for a valuation or an amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the request or order ask for a valuation (paragraphs (2) to (4)) or for the amount of the former Category A pension (paragraph (5))?
      `I told the Secretary of State by then that the information is needed for proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By the date the Secretary of State received the request or order, did you notify the Secretary of State that the information is needed in connection with proceedings already started?
      `the court set a shorter period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the court set a shorter period in an order?
      `the last day of the shorter period the court set` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the last day of that period? (Give any date if there is none.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must the Secretary of State give me the information that has been asked for` IS
    `inserted regulation 6(7) and (8): the last day by which the Secretary of State must furnish the information` `the request`
    WHERE
        `the request` MEANS InformationRequest WITH
            `who makes the request or order` IS `who makes the request`
            `the date the Secretary of State receives the request or order` IS `the date the Secretary of State receives the request or order`
            `the request or order asks for a valuation under paragraphs (2) to (4) or an amount under paragraph (5)` IS `the request or order asks for a valuation or an amount`
            `the person notified the Secretary of State by that date that the information is needed in connection with proceedings under a provision referred to in section 23(1)(a) of the 1999 Act` IS `I told the Secretary of State by then that the information is needed for proceedings`
            `the last day of any shorter period the court has specified in an order, if any` IS IF `the court set a shorter period` THEN JUST `the last day of the shorter period the court set` ELSE NOTHING

-- Inserted reg 7. Where an application for financial relief or provision has been made or is in contemplation.
@export Is the valuation I am given calculated and verified on the Government Actuary's guidance (inserted reg 7)?
GIVEN `an application for financial relief or financial provision has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application for financial relief or financial provision been made?
      `such an application is in contemplation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is such an application in contemplation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the valuation I am given calculated and verified on the Government Actuary's guidance` IF
    `inserted regulation 7: the valuation is calculated and verified in accordance with the Government Actuary's guidance` `an application for financial relief or financial provision has been made` `such an application is in contemplation`


-- Regulations 15 to 20. A situation: ask "Has your spouse or civil partner died?" before showing this group.
-- The rate of the deceased's graduated retirement benefit, and the dates of their death and pensionable age, are facts the person states.
§§ `If my husband, wife or civil partner has died: my inherited pension (regs 15 to 20)`

-- Reg 16(1) to (3). (1): the spouse died before 6 April 2016 and the person was under pensionable age and has not married again; (2): the spouse reached pensionable age before
-- 6 April 2016 but died on or after it, the same conditions; (3): the same spouse facts, the person over pensionable age when they died. 'Under' and 'over' are strict, so on the day
-- the person reaches pensionable age they are neither (fork F20): NOTHING.
@export Which paragraph of regulation 16 gives me an inherited amount (reg 16)?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking about?
      `the date I reach pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you reach, or did you reach, State Pension age?
      `how my spouse or civil partner and I were related` IS A KindOfRelationship @desc Were you and the person who died married to each other, or civil partners of each other?
      `my spouse or civil partner died while we were married or civil partners of each other` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your spouse or civil partner die while the two of you were still married, or still civil partners, to each other?
      `either of us was married to someone else when they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When they died, was either of you married to a third person?
      `the date my spouse or civil partner died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your spouse or civil partner die?
      `I married or formed a civil partnership again before reaching pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Between their death and the date you reached State Pension age, did you marry or form a civil partnership?
      `the date my spouse or civil partner reached pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your spouse or civil partner reach State Pension age?
GIVETH A MAYBE InheritedAmountCase
DECIDE `Which paragraph of regulation 16 gives me an inherited amount` IS
    `regulation 16: which paragraph gives the person an inherited amount` `my facts` `my late spouse`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS SpouseDeathFacts WITH
            `the day on which the question is asked` IS `the day I am asking about`
            `the date the person reaches pensionable age` IS `the date I reach pensionable age`
            `the kind of relationship` IS `how my spouse or civil partner and I were related`
            `the spouse or civil partner died while the two were married or civil partners of each other` IS `my spouse or civil partner died while we were married or civil partners of each other`
            `either of them was married to a third person at the time of the death` IS `either of us was married to someone else when they died`
            `the date the spouse or civil partner died` IS `the date my spouse or civil partner died`
            `the person has married or formed a civil partnership between the date of death and the date they reached pensionable age` IS `I married or formed a civil partnership again before reaching pensionable age`
        `my late spouse` MEANS InheritedAmountFacts WITH
            `the date the spouse or civil partner reached pensionable age` IS `the date my spouse or civil partner reached pensionable age`
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read the rate.
            `the weekly rate of the deceased's graduated retirement benefit, determined in accordance with regulation 16(5)` IS 0

-- Reg 16(6). For paragraphs (1) and (2), the date I reach pensionable age; for paragraph (3), the date they died. NOTHING where no paragraph of reg 16 applies.
@export On what date is the rate of my late spouse's or civil partner's benefit fixed (reg 16(6))?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking about?
      `the date I reach pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you reach, or did you reach, State Pension age?
      `how my spouse or civil partner and I were related` IS A KindOfRelationship @desc Were you and the person who died married to each other, or civil partners of each other?
      `my spouse or civil partner died while we were married or civil partners of each other` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your spouse or civil partner die while the two of you were still married, or still civil partners, to each other?
      `either of us was married to someone else when they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When they died, was either of you married to a third person?
      `the date my spouse or civil partner died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your spouse or civil partner die?
      `I married or formed a civil partnership again before reaching pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Between their death and the date you reached State Pension age, did you marry or form a civil partnership?
      `the date my spouse or civil partner reached pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your spouse or civil partner reach State Pension age?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what date is the rate of my late spouse's or civil partner's benefit fixed` IS
    CONSIDER `regulation 16: which paragraph gives the person an inherited amount` `my facts` `my late spouse`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST paragraph THEN JUST (`regulation 16(6): the date as at which the deceased's graduated retirement benefit rate is determined` `my facts` paragraph)
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS SpouseDeathFacts WITH
            `the day on which the question is asked` IS `the day I am asking about`
            `the date the person reaches pensionable age` IS `the date I reach pensionable age`
            `the kind of relationship` IS `how my spouse or civil partner and I were related`
            `the spouse or civil partner died while the two were married or civil partners of each other` IS `my spouse or civil partner died while we were married or civil partners of each other`
            `either of them was married to a third person at the time of the death` IS `either of us was married to someone else when they died`
            `the date the spouse or civil partner died` IS `the date my spouse or civil partner died`
            `the person has married or formed a civil partnership between the date of death and the date they reached pensionable age` IS `I married or formed a civil partnership again before reaching pensionable age`
        `my late spouse` MEANS InheritedAmountFacts WITH
            `the date the spouse or civil partner reached pensionable age` IS `the date my spouse or civil partner reached pensionable age`
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read the rate.
            `the weekly rate of the deceased's graduated retirement benefit, determined in accordance with regulation 16(5)` IS 0

-- Reg 16(4). Half of the weekly rate of the deceased's graduated retirement benefit.
@export How much a week is my inherited amount, in pounds (reg 16(4))?
GIVEN `the weekly rate of my spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the weekly rate, in pounds, of your spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit, worked out as regulation 16(5) says?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much a week is my inherited amount, in pounds` IS
    `regulation 16(4): the inherited amount, in pounds per week` `my late spouse`
    WHERE
        `my late spouse` MEANS InheritedAmountFacts WITH
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read the date.
            `the date the spouse or civil partner reached pensionable age` IS (YMD 2000 1 1)
            `the weekly rate of the deceased's graduated retirement benefit, determined in accordance with regulation 16(5)` IS `the weekly rate of my spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit`

-- Reg 15(2). I have reached pensionable age; they died while we were married or civil partners (reg 1(5) applies to marriage); the marriage or civil partnership
-- before 6 April 2016; and I am entitled to an inherited amount under reg 16.
@export Am I entitled to a survivor's State Pension based on my late spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit (reg 15(2))?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking about?
      `the date I reach pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you reach, or did you reach, State Pension age?
      `how my spouse or civil partner and I were related` IS A KindOfRelationship @desc Were you and the person who died married to each other, or civil partners of each other?
      `my spouse or civil partner died while we were married or civil partners of each other` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your spouse or civil partner die while the two of you were still married, or still civil partners, to each other?
      `either of us was married to someone else when they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When they died, was either of you married to a third person?
      `the date my spouse or civil partner died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your spouse or civil partner die?
      `I married or formed a civil partnership again before reaching pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Between their death and the date you reached State Pension age, did you marry or form a civil partnership?
      `the date my spouse or civil partner reached pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your spouse or civil partner reach State Pension age?
      `the date I married or formed the civil partnership` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you marry, or form the civil partnership?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to a survivor's State Pension based on my late spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit` IF
    `regulation 15(2): the person is entitled to a state pension under regulation 15` `my facts` `my late spouse` `my marriage`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS SpouseDeathFacts WITH
            `the day on which the question is asked` IS `the day I am asking about`
            `the date the person reaches pensionable age` IS `the date I reach pensionable age`
            `the kind of relationship` IS `how my spouse or civil partner and I were related`
            `the spouse or civil partner died while the two were married or civil partners of each other` IS `my spouse or civil partner died while we were married or civil partners of each other`
            `either of them was married to a third person at the time of the death` IS `either of us was married to someone else when they died`
            `the date the spouse or civil partner died` IS `the date my spouse or civil partner died`
            `the person has married or formed a civil partnership between the date of death and the date they reached pensionable age` IS `I married or formed a civil partnership again before reaching pensionable age`
        `my late spouse` MEANS InheritedAmountFacts WITH
            `the date the spouse or civil partner reached pensionable age` IS `the date my spouse or civil partner reached pensionable age`
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read the rate.
            `the weekly rate of the deceased's graduated retirement benefit, determined in accordance with regulation 16(5)` IS 0
        `my marriage` MEANS MarriageFacts WITH
            `the date the marriage took place or the civil partnership was formed` IS `the date I married or formed the civil partnership`

-- Reg 15(3). The inherited amount; NOTHING where there is no inherited amount.
@export What weekly rate of survivor's State Pension do I get under regulation 15, in pounds (reg 15(3))?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking about?
      `the date I reach pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you reach, or did you reach, State Pension age?
      `how my spouse or civil partner and I were related` IS A KindOfRelationship @desc Were you and the person who died married to each other, or civil partners of each other?
      `my spouse or civil partner died while we were married or civil partners of each other` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your spouse or civil partner die while the two of you were still married, or still civil partners, to each other?
      `either of us was married to someone else when they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When they died, was either of you married to a third person?
      `the date my spouse or civil partner died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your spouse or civil partner die?
      `I married or formed a civil partnership again before reaching pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Between their death and the date you reached State Pension age, did you marry or form a civil partnership?
      `the date my spouse or civil partner reached pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your spouse or civil partner reach State Pension age?
      `the weekly rate of my spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the weekly rate, in pounds, of your spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit, worked out as regulation 16(5) says?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What weekly rate of survivor's State Pension do I get under regulation 15, in pounds` IS
    `regulation 15(3): the weekly rate of the state pension under regulation 15` `my facts` `my late spouse`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS SpouseDeathFacts WITH
            `the day on which the question is asked` IS `the day I am asking about`
            `the date the person reaches pensionable age` IS `the date I reach pensionable age`
            `the kind of relationship` IS `how my spouse or civil partner and I were related`
            `the spouse or civil partner died while the two were married or civil partners of each other` IS `my spouse or civil partner died while we were married or civil partners of each other`
            `either of them was married to a third person at the time of the death` IS `either of us was married to someone else when they died`
            `the date the spouse or civil partner died` IS `the date my spouse or civil partner died`
            `the person has married or formed a civil partnership between the date of death and the date they reached pensionable age` IS `I married or formed a civil partnership again before reaching pensionable age`
        `my late spouse` MEANS InheritedAmountFacts WITH
            `the date the spouse or civil partner reached pensionable age` IS `the date my spouse or civil partner reached pensionable age`
            `the weekly rate of the deceased's graduated retirement benefit, determined in accordance with regulation 16(5)` IS `the weekly rate of my spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit`

-- Reg 17. R is my regulation 15 rate, S the rate of my other State Pension under sections 7 and 2, 4 or 12, F the full rate. If R+S is at most F the full-rate percentage applies to R; if R+S exceeds F but
-- S is below F, the full-rate percentage applies to the shortfall (F minus S) and the up-rating order's percentage to the excess (R+S minus F), and both add; if S is at least F only an order applies, to R.
-- Where R+S is at most F, an order alone gives nothing.
@export By how much is my regulation 15 State Pension increased, in pounds a week (reg 17)?
GIVEN `the weekly rate of my regulation 15 State Pension` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly rate, in pounds, of your State Pension under regulation 15, without any increase under section 17 of the 2014 Act?
      `the weekly rate of my other State Pension` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total weekly rate, in pounds, of any other State Pension you are entitled to under section 7 and section 2, 4 or 12 of the 2014 Act?
      `the full weekly rate of the State Pension` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the full weekly rate of the State Pension, in pounds, at that time?
      `the full rate was increased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the full rate of the State Pension increased?
      `the percentage the full rate was increased by` IS A NUMBER @desc By what percentage? (For 10%, enter 10. Enter 0 if it was not.)
      `an up-rating order came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did an up-rating order under section 151A of the Administration Act come into force?
      `the percentage the order specifies` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage does the order specify? (For 5%, enter 5. Enter 0 if there was none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `By how much is my regulation 15 State Pension increased, in pounds a week` IS
    `regulation 17: the increase in the rate of the state pension under regulation 15` `the weekly rate of my regulation 15 State Pension` `the weekly rate of my other State Pension` `the full weekly rate of the State Pension`
        (IF `the full rate was increased` THEN JUST ((`the percentage the full rate was increased by`) %) ELSE NOTHING)
        (IF `an up-rating order came into force` THEN JUST ((`the percentage the order specifies`) %) ELSE NOTHING)

-- Reg 18(1), (8). I have reached pensionable age; they died while married or civil partners; their benefit was deferred at death and throughout the 12 months before;
-- and I was under pensionable age when they died and did not marry again before reaching it, or was over it. Not if I already have a choice under section 8(2) of the 2014 Act.
@export Am I entitled to choose between a lump sum and a State Pension based on my late spouse's deferred benefit (reg 18(1), (8))?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking about?
      `the date I reach pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you reach, or did you reach, State Pension age?
      `how my spouse or civil partner and I were related` IS A KindOfRelationship @desc Were you and the person who died married to each other, or civil partners of each other?
      `my spouse or civil partner died while we were married or civil partners of each other` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your spouse or civil partner die while the two of you were still married, or still civil partners, to each other?
      `either of us was married to someone else when they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When they died, was either of you married to a third person?
      `the date my spouse or civil partner died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your spouse or civil partner die?
      `I married or formed a civil partnership again before reaching pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Between their death and the date you reached State Pension age, did you marry or form a civil partnership?
      `my spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit was deferred when they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit deferred when they died?
      `it was deferred throughout the 12 months before they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it deferred throughout the 12 months ending with the day before they died?
      `I am entitled to a choice under section 8(2) of the 2014 Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to a choice under section 8(2) of the Pensions Act 2014?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to choose between a lump sum and a State Pension based on my late spouse's deferred benefit` IF
    `regulation 18(1) and (8): the person is entitled to a choice under regulation 18` `my facts` `my deferred benefit`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS SpouseDeathFacts WITH
            `the day on which the question is asked` IS `the day I am asking about`
            `the date the person reaches pensionable age` IS `the date I reach pensionable age`
            `the kind of relationship` IS `how my spouse or civil partner and I were related`
            `the spouse or civil partner died while the two were married or civil partners of each other` IS `my spouse or civil partner died while we were married or civil partners of each other`
            `either of them was married to a third person at the time of the death` IS `either of us was married to someone else when they died`
            `the date the spouse or civil partner died` IS `the date my spouse or civil partner died`
            `the person has married or formed a civil partnership between the date of death and the date they reached pensionable age` IS `I married or formed a civil partnership again before reaching pensionable age`
        `my deferred benefit` MEANS DeferredGrbFacts WITH
            `the spouse's or civil partner's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred at the time of death` IS `my spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit was deferred when they died`
            `it was deferred throughout the period of 12 months ending with the day before the death` IS `it was deferred throughout the 12 months before they died`
            `the person is entitled to a choice under section 8(2) of the 2014 Act` IS `I am entitled to a choice under section 8(2) of the 2014 Act`

-- Reg 18(1) with 19(2). Taken as the later of the date I reach pensionable age and the date they died (fork F22).
@export On what date do I become entitled to make that choice (reg 18(1))?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking about?
      `the date I reach pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you reach, or did you reach, State Pension age?
      `how my spouse or civil partner and I were related` IS A KindOfRelationship @desc Were you and the person who died married to each other, or civil partners of each other?
      `my spouse or civil partner died while we were married or civil partners of each other` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your spouse or civil partner die while the two of you were still married, or still civil partners, to each other?
      `either of us was married to someone else when they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When they died, was either of you married to a third person?
      `the date my spouse or civil partner died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your spouse or civil partner die?
      `I married or formed a civil partnership again before reaching pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Between their death and the date you reached State Pension age, did you marry or form a civil partnership?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what date do I become entitled to make that choice` IS
    `regulation 18(1): the date on which the person becomes entitled to make the choice` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS SpouseDeathFacts WITH
            `the day on which the question is asked` IS `the day I am asking about`
            `the date the person reaches pensionable age` IS `the date I reach pensionable age`
            `the kind of relationship` IS `how my spouse or civil partner and I were related`
            `the spouse or civil partner died while the two were married or civil partners of each other` IS `my spouse or civil partner died while we were married or civil partners of each other`
            `either of them was married to a third person at the time of the death` IS `either of us was married to someone else when they died`
            `the date the spouse or civil partner died` IS `the date my spouse or civil partner died`
            `the person has married or formed a civil partnership between the date of death and the date they reached pensionable age` IS `I married or formed a civil partnership again before reaching pensionable age`

-- Reg 19(2). The date I become entitled to make a choice under reg 18.
@export Which date is read as the date I became entitled when my lump sum is worked out (reg 19(2))?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking about?
      `the date I reach pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you reach, or did you reach, State Pension age?
      `how my spouse or civil partner and I were related` IS A KindOfRelationship @desc Were you and the person who died married to each other, or civil partners of each other?
      `my spouse or civil partner died while we were married or civil partners of each other` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your spouse or civil partner die while the two of you were still married, or still civil partners, to each other?
      `either of us was married to someone else when they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When they died, was either of you married to a third person?
      `the date my spouse or civil partner died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your spouse or civil partner die?
      `I married or formed a civil partnership again before reaching pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Between their death and the date you reached State Pension age, did you marry or form a civil partnership?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Which date is read as the date I became entitled when my lump sum is worked out` IS
    `regulation 19(2): the date read in place of the date of becoming entitled to a retirement pension or graduated retirement benefit` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS SpouseDeathFacts WITH
            `the day on which the question is asked` IS `the day I am asking about`
            `the date the person reaches pensionable age` IS `the date I reach pensionable age`
            `the kind of relationship` IS `how my spouse or civil partner and I were related`
            `the spouse or civil partner died while the two were married or civil partners of each other` IS `my spouse or civil partner died while we were married or civil partners of each other`
            `either of them was married to a third person at the time of the death` IS `either of us was married to someone else when they died`
            `the date the spouse or civil partner died` IS `the date my spouse or civil partner died`
            `the person has married or formed a civil partnership between the date of death and the date they reached pensionable age` IS `I married or formed a civil partnership again before reaching pensionable age`

-- Reg 18(4) applying reg 4(2), (3). Same period as for a section 8 choice.
@export Is my choice under regulation 18 made in time (reg 18(4))?
GIVEN `I was sent a notice confirming that I may make the choice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Secretary of State send you a notice confirming that you may make the choice?
      `the date in the most recent such notice` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the date in the most recent such notice? (Give any date if you got none.)
      `the date I claimed my State Pension` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you claim your State Pension?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking about?
      `the date I reach pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you reach, or did you reach, State Pension age?
      `how my spouse or civil partner and I were related` IS A KindOfRelationship @desc Were you and the person who died married to each other, or civil partners of each other?
      `my spouse or civil partner died while we were married or civil partners of each other` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your spouse or civil partner die while the two of you were still married, or still civil partners, to each other?
      `either of us was married to someone else when they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When they died, was either of you married to a third person?
      `the date my spouse or civil partner died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your spouse or civil partner die?
      `I married or formed a civil partnership again before reaching pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Between their death and the date you reached State Pension age, did you marry or form a civil partnership?
      `the date I make my choice` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you make (or did you make) your choice?
GIVETH A ChoiceTiming
DECIDE `Is my choice under regulation 18 made in time` IS
    `regulation 18(4): whether the choice is made within the period` (IF `I was sent a notice confirming that I may make the choice` THEN JUST `the date in the most recent such notice` ELSE NOTHING) `the date I claimed my State Pension` `my facts` `the date I make my choice`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS SpouseDeathFacts WITH
            `the day on which the question is asked` IS `the day I am asking about`
            `the date the person reaches pensionable age` IS `the date I reach pensionable age`
            `the kind of relationship` IS `how my spouse or civil partner and I were related`
            `the spouse or civil partner died while the two were married or civil partners of each other` IS `my spouse or civil partner died while we were married or civil partners of each other`
            `either of them was married to a third person at the time of the death` IS `either of us was married to someone else when they died`
            `the date the spouse or civil partner died` IS `the date my spouse or civil partner died`
            `the person has married or formed a civil partnership between the date of death and the date they reached pensionable age` IS `I married or formed a civil partnership again before reaching pensionable age`

-- Reg 18(4). Same conditions as for a late section 8 choice.
@export May I still make a late choice under regulation 18 (reg 18(4))?
GIVEN `the Secretary of State considers it reasonable to let me choose late` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Secretary of State consider it reasonable, in your case, to let you choose late?
      `an amount has been paid to me as, or on account of, a lump sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has any amount been paid to you as, or on account of, a lump sum under regulation 19?
      `I have repaid that amount to the Secretary of State in full` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you repaid that amount to the Secretary of State in full?
      `I repaid it in the currency in which it was paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you repay it in the currency in which it was originally paid?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I still make a late choice under regulation 18` IF
    `regulation 18(4): a late choice may be made` `my late choice facts`
    WHERE
        `my late choice facts` MEANS LateChoiceFacts WITH
            `the Secretary of State considers it reasonable in the particular case` IS `the Secretary of State considers it reasonable to let me choose late`
            `an amount has been paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum under section 8(4) of the 2014 Act` IS `an amount has been paid to me as, or on account of, a lump sum`
            `that amount has been repaid to the Secretary of State in full` IS `I have repaid that amount to the Secretary of State in full`
            `that amount has been repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid` IS `I repaid it in the currency in which it was paid`

-- Reg 18(6). The lump sum falls to nil where the person makes a late choice to be paid a state pension under reg 20.
@export How much lump sum am I paid if I make a late choice of a State Pension under regulation 18, in pounds (reg 18(6))?
GIVEN `the lump sum I would otherwise be paid` IS A NUMBER @desc What lump sum, in pounds, would you otherwise be paid under regulation 19?
      `I make a late choice to be paid a State Pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you making a late choice to be paid a State Pension under regulation 20 instead?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much lump sum am I paid if I make a late choice of a State Pension under regulation 18, in pounds` IS
    `regulation 18(6): the amount of the lump sum` `the lump sum I would otherwise be paid` `I make a late choice to be paid a State Pension`

-- Reg 18(2), (5), (9) to (11). A choice made in time stands; an allowed alteration replaces it; a refused alteration leaves it; no choice, or none in time, means a lump sum.
-- Not covered where paragraph (1) does not apply.
@export Am I paid a lump sum or a State Pension under regulation 18 (reg 18(2), (5), (9) to (11))?
GIVEN `regulation 18(1) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 18(1) apply to you (see the question about being entitled to choose)?
      `I made a choice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made a choice between a lump sum and a State Pension?
      `the choice I made` IS A PaymentChoice @desc Which did you choose: a lump sum, or a state pension? (Choose either if you made none.)
      `my choice was made in the manner required and in time, or is a late choice that may be made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your choice made in the manner required and in time (or is it a late choice that may be made)?
      `I ask to change my choice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you ask to change your choice?
      `the choice I ask to change to` IS A PaymentChoice @desc Which do you ask to change to? (Choose either if you do not.)
      `my choice may be altered under regulation 6` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May your choice be altered under regulation 6 (see the question about changing a choice)?
GIVETH A PaymentOutcome
DECIDE `Am I paid a lump sum or a State Pension under regulation 18` IS
    `regulation 18: what the person is to be paid` `my outcome facts`
    WHERE
        `my outcome facts` MEANS GrbChoiceOutcomeFacts WITH
            `paragraph (1) applies to the person` IS `regulation 18(1) applies to me`
            `the choice the person made, if any` IS IF `I made a choice` THEN JUST `the choice I made` ELSE NOTHING
            `the choice was made in the manner required and within the period, or is a late choice that may be made` IS `my choice was made in the manner required and in time, or is a late choice that may be made`
            `the choice the person asks to change to, if any` IS IF `I ask to change my choice` THEN JUST `the choice I ask to change to` ELSE NOTHING
            `the choice may be altered under regulation 6` IS `my choice may be altered under regulation 6`

-- Reg 19(1). A lump sum calculated under paragraph 10 or 20 of Schedule 1 to the 2005 Regulations (not an input: the figure is supplied). NOTHING unless regulation 18 gives a lump sum.
@export How much lump sum am I paid under regulation 19, in pounds (reg 19(1))?
GIVEN `what regulation 18 gives me` IS A PaymentOutcome @desc What does regulation 18 give you: a lump sum, a State Pension, or does it not cover you?
      `the lump sum calculated under the 2005 Regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc What lump sum, in pounds, is calculated under paragraph 10 or 20 of Schedule 1 to the Social Security (Graduated Retirement Benefit) Regulations 2005?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much lump sum am I paid under regulation 19, in pounds` IS
    `regulation 19(1): the lump sum payable` `what regulation 18 gives me` `the lump sum calculated under the 2005 Regulations`

-- Reg 20(1). (a)-(c) as for reg 18, (d) they were entitled to an increase or their benefit was deferred when they died, and (e), (f) where reg 18 applies, the outcome must be a State Pension.
-- Where reg 18 does not cover the person, (e) and (f) do not arise.
@export Am I entitled to a survivor's State Pension based on my late spouse's deferred or increased graduated retirement benefit (reg 20(1))?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking about?
      `the date I reach pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you reach, or did you reach, State Pension age?
      `how my spouse or civil partner and I were related` IS A KindOfRelationship @desc Were you and the person who died married to each other, or civil partners of each other?
      `my spouse or civil partner died while we were married or civil partners of each other` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your spouse or civil partner die while the two of you were still married, or still civil partners, to each other?
      `either of us was married to someone else when they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When they died, was either of you married to a third person?
      `the date my spouse or civil partner died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your spouse or civil partner die?
      `I married or formed a civil partnership again before reaching pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Between their death and the date you reached State Pension age, did you marry or form a civil partnership?
      `my spouse or civil partner was entitled to an increase in graduated retirement benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your spouse or civil partner entitled to an increase in graduated retirement benefit?
      `my spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit was deferred when they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was their graduated retirement benefit deferred when they died?
      `what regulation 18 gives me` IS A PaymentOutcome @desc What does regulation 18 give you: a lump sum, a State Pension, or does it not cover you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to a survivor's State Pension based on my late spouse's deferred or increased graduated retirement benefit` IF
    `regulation 20(1): the person is entitled to a state pension under regulation 20` `my facts` `my increase facts` `what regulation 18 gives me`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS SpouseDeathFacts WITH
            `the day on which the question is asked` IS `the day I am asking about`
            `the date the person reaches pensionable age` IS `the date I reach pensionable age`
            `the kind of relationship` IS `how my spouse or civil partner and I were related`
            `the spouse or civil partner died while the two were married or civil partners of each other` IS `my spouse or civil partner died while we were married or civil partners of each other`
            `either of them was married to a third person at the time of the death` IS `either of us was married to someone else when they died`
            `the date the spouse or civil partner died` IS `the date my spouse or civil partner died`
            `the person has married or formed a civil partnership between the date of death and the date they reached pensionable age` IS `I married or formed a civil partnership again before reaching pensionable age`
        `my increase facts` MEANS IncreaseFacts WITH
            `the spouse or civil partner was entitled to an increase in graduated retirement benefit` IS `my spouse or civil partner was entitled to an increase in graduated retirement benefit`
            `the spouse's or civil partner's entitlement to graduated retirement benefit was deferred when they died` IS `my spouse's or civil partner's graduated retirement benefit was deferred when they died`

-- Reg 20(2). Half the weekly rate of my late spouse's or civil partner's increase in graduated retirement benefit (the rate they would have had if the deferral ended just before death).
@export What weekly rate of State Pension do I get under regulation 20, in pounds (reg 20(2))?
GIVEN `the weekly rate of my spouse's or civil partner's increase in graduated retirement benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the weekly rate, in pounds, of your spouse's or civil partner's increase in graduated retirement benefit, worked out as regulation 20(4) says?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What weekly rate of State Pension do I get under regulation 20, in pounds` IS
    `regulation 20(2): the weekly rate of the state pension under regulation 20` `the weekly rate of my spouse's or civil partner's increase in graduated retirement benefit`

-- Reg 20(3). Increased at the time of the order by the percentage the order specifies.
@export What is my regulation 20 State Pension after an up-rating order, in pounds a week (reg 20(3))?
GIVEN `the rate of my State Pension under regulation 20` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly rate, in pounds, of your State Pension under regulation 20?
      `the percentage the order specifies` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage does the up-rating order specify? (For 5%, enter 5.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my regulation 20 State Pension after an up-rating order, in pounds a week` IS
    `regulation 20(3): the rate after an order under section 151A of the Administration Act` `the rate of my State Pension under regulation 20` ((`the percentage the order specifies`) %)


-- Regulations 21 to 23. A situation: ask "Do you live, or have you lived, outside the United Kingdom?" before showing this group.
§§ `If I live abroad (regs 21 to 23)`

-- Reg 21. Where regulations apply reg 21 to an up-rating increase (taken as an input, fork F25), a person who was entitled to a State Pension and an overseas resident just before the increase gets none;
-- for a person whose pension was deferred, and who was entitled and overseas when the deferral ended, none for an increase during the deferral if overseas throughout, and none after it if overseas then.
@export Is my up-rating increase taken away because I live overseas (reg 21)?
GIVEN `regulations apply regulation 21 to this up-rating increase` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have regulations been made saying that regulation 21 applies to this up-rating increase?
      `the date the up-rating increase comes into force` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the up-rating increase come into force?
      `my State Pension was deferred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your State Pension ever deferred?
      `the first day of my deferral` IS A DATE @desc If so, what was the first day of your deferral? (Give any date if not.)
      `the last day of my deferral` IS A DATE @desc If so, what was the last day of your deferral? (Give any date if not.)
      `when my deferral ended I was entitled to a State Pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your State Pension was deferred: when the deferral ended, were you entitled to a State Pension under Part 1 of the Pensions Act 2014?
      `when my deferral ended I was an overseas resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your State Pension was deferred: when the deferral ended, were you an overseas resident?
      `I am entitled to a State Pension immediately before the increase` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to a State Pension under Part 1 of the Pensions Act 2014 immediately before the increase comes into force?
      `I am an overseas resident when the increase comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an overseas resident when the increase comes into force?
      `I stayed an overseas resident until my deferral ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your State Pension was deferred: did you stay an overseas resident until the deferral ended?
GIVETH A UpratingOutcome
DECIDE `Is my up-rating increase taken away because I live overseas` IS
    `regulation 21: whether the person is entitled to the up-rating increase` `my overseas facts`
    WHERE
        `my deferral` MEANS DeferralPeriod WITH
            `first day of the deferral` IS `the first day of my deferral`
            `last day of the deferral` IS `the last day of my deferral`
        `my overseas facts` MEANS OverseasFacts WITH
            `regulations have been made providing that regulation 21 applies to this up-rating increase` IS `regulations apply regulation 21 to this up-rating increase`
            `the date the up-rating increase comes into force` IS `the date the up-rating increase comes into force`
            `when the deferral period ended the person was entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act` IS `when my deferral ended I was entitled to a State Pension`
            `when the deferral period ended the person was an overseas resident` IS `when my deferral ended I was an overseas resident`
            `the person is entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act immediately before the increase comes into force` IS `I am entitled to a State Pension immediately before the increase`
            `the person is an overseas resident at the time the increase comes into force` IS `I am an overseas resident when the increase comes into force`
            `the person continued to be an overseas resident until the deferral period ended` IS `I stayed an overseas resident until my deferral ended`
            `the period of deferral, if the person's entitlement was ever deferred` IS IF `my State Pension was deferred` THEN JUST `my deferral` ELSE NOTHING

-- Reg 21(6). Any part of the Channel Islands not covered by an Order under section 179 of the Administration Act is a specified territory.
@export Is the place where I live a territory specified for the State Pension (reg 21(6))?
GIVEN `the place is in the Channel Islands` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place where you live in the Channel Islands?
      `the place is subject to an Order under section 179 of the Administration Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it covered by an Order made under section 179 of the Social Security Administration Act 1992?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the place where I live a territory specified for the State Pension` IF
    `regulation 21(6): the place is a territory specified for sections 18(4) and 20(2) and (3) of the 2014 Act` `the place is in the Channel Islands` `the place is subject to an Order under section 179 of the Administration Act`

-- Reg 22(1). It applies if the person was an overseas resident for any part of the deferral period. One flag is asked in place of a list of parts: 'any part' is exact for it.
@export Does regulation 22 apply to me because I was an overseas resident during my deferral (reg 22(1))?
GIVEN `I was an overseas resident for some part of my deferral` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you an overseas resident for any part of the period your State Pension was deferred?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does regulation 22 apply to me because I was an overseas resident during my deferral` IF
    `regulation 22(1): regulation 22 applies` (LIST `my part`)
    WHERE
        `my part` MEANS PartOfDeferral WITH
            `the person was an overseas resident during the part` IS `I was an overseas resident for some part of my deferral`
            -- Placeholder: regulation 22(1) does not read this field.
            `the person was in Great Britain or a territory specified in regulation 21(6) during the part` IS FALSE

-- Reg 22(2), (3) and, where 12A also applies, 23(4). Overseas and outside Great Britain and the specified territories: the rate just before the START of the part; not overseas: just before the END;
-- overseas but in Great Britain or a specified territory: neither paragraph says (fork F27).
@export On which weekly rate is my increment for this part of my deferral worked (regs 22(2), (3), 23(4))?
GIVEN `I was an overseas resident during that part of my deferral` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During that part of your deferral, were you an overseas resident?
      `I was in Great Britain or a specified territory during that part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During that part, were you in Great Britain or in a territory specified in regulation 21(6)?
GIVETH A ReferenceRate
DECIDE `On which weekly rate is my increment for this part of my deferral worked` IS
    `regulation 22(2) and (3): the rate on which the increment for the part is worked` `my part`
    WHERE
        `my part` MEANS PartOfDeferral WITH
            `the person was an overseas resident during the part` IS `I was an overseas resident during that part of my deferral`
            `the person was in Great Britain or a territory specified in regulation 21(6) during the part` IS `I was in Great Britain or a specified territory during that part`

-- Reg 22. One-ninth of 1% of the weekly rate the paragraphs choose, for each whole week counted in the part. How the counted weeks are shared among the parts is not said (fork F16).
@export What is my increment for this part of my deferral, in pounds a week (reg 22)?
GIVEN `I was an overseas resident during that part of my deferral` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During that part of your deferral, were you an overseas resident?
      `I was in Great Britain or a specified territory during that part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During that part, were you in Great Britain or in a territory specified in regulation 21(6)?
      `the whole weeks counted in that part` IS A NUMBER @desc How many whole weeks count in that part?
      `my weekly rate immediately before the start of that part` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your weekly rate of State Pension, in pounds, immediately before that part began?
      `my weekly rate immediately before the end of that part` IS A NUMBER @desc What was it immediately before that part ended?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my increment for this part of my deferral, in pounds a week` IS
    `regulation 22: the increment for the part` `my part` `the whole weeks counted in that part` `my weekly rate immediately before the start of that part` `my weekly rate immediately before the end of that part`
    WHERE
        `my part` MEANS PartOfDeferral WITH
            `the person was an overseas resident during the part` IS `I was an overseas resident during that part of my deferral`
            `the person was in Great Britain or a territory specified in regulation 21(6) during the part` IS `I was in Great Britain or a specified territory during that part`

-- Reg 23(1). 12A applies where the weekly rate would have changed other than by up-rating during the deferral, and 22 where the person was overseas for any part. A single change date is asked about.
@export Do regulations 12A and 22 both apply to my deferral (reg 23(1))?
GIVEN `the first day of my deferral` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of your deferral?
      `the last day of my deferral` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of your deferral?
      `my weekly rate would have changed during the deferral other than by up-rating` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During the deferral, would your weekly rate of State Pension have changed for a reason other than an up-rating increase?
      `the date of that change` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (Give any date if no.)
      `I was an overseas resident for some part of my deferral` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you an overseas resident for any part of the deferral?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do regulations 12A and 22 both apply to my deferral` IF
    `regulation 23(1): regulations 12A and 22 both apply` `my deferral` (IF `my weekly rate would have changed during the deferral other than by up-rating` THEN LIST `the date of that change` ELSE EMPTY) (LIST `my part`)
    WHERE
        `my deferral` MEANS DeferralPeriod WITH
            `first day of the deferral` IS `the first day of my deferral`
            `last day of the deferral` IS `the last day of my deferral`
        `my part` MEANS PartOfDeferral WITH
            `the person was an overseas resident during the part` IS `I was an overseas resident for some part of my deferral`
            -- Placeholder: regulation 22(1) does not read this field.
            `the person was in Great Britain or a territory specified in regulation 21(6) during the part` IS FALSE

-- Reg 23(3), (5). The increment under reg 22, plus the increase (or less the decrease) that reg 12A makes with the paragraph (4) rate. What that increase is measured against is not said (fork F24): it is taken as the difference reg 12A makes.
@export What is my increment where regulations 12A and 22 both apply, in pounds a week (reg 23(5))?
GIVEN `my increment under regulation 22` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your increment, in pounds, worked out under regulation 22?
      `the increase or decrease that regulation 12A makes` IS A NUMBER @desc By how much, in pounds, does regulation 12A, using the rate from regulation 23(4), increase it? (Enter a minus number for a decrease.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my increment where regulations 12A and 22 both apply, in pounds a week` IS
    `regulation 23(5): the increment where regulations 12A and 22 both apply` `my increment under regulation 22` `the increase or decrease that regulation 12A makes`


-- Part 8. A credit is a week treated as if contributions (or earnings) had been paid, so that the year can count as a qualifying year. A situation: ask
-- "Were you out of work, caring, bringing up a child, fostering, abroad with a member of the forces, or receiving a benefit, in a year you want to count?" before showing this group.
§§ `National Insurance credits towards my State Pension (regs 24 to 39)`


§§§ `Which rules cover which weeks (regs 24, 25)`

-- Reg 24(2). Nothing in Chapter 3 credits any day, or any event, before 6 April 2016.
@export Can credits under Chapter 3 reach this day (reg 24(2))?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can credits under Chapter 3 reach this day` IF
    `regulation 24(2): Chapter 3 can credit the day` `the day I am asking about`

-- Reg 25(1), (3). A week that falls partly in two tax years counts in the year in which it begins. Chapter 2 is for a year before 6 April 2016, Chapter 3 for any other (fork F28).
@export Which Chapter of Part 8 covers the week I am asking about (reg 25(1), (3))?
GIVEN `the first day of the week I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the week you are asking about?
GIVETH A CreditChapter
DECIDE `Which Chapter of Part 8 covers the week I am asking about` IS
    `regulation 25(1): the Chapter that makes provision for the week` `the first day of the week I am asking about`

-- Reg 25(2). A person is credited only as much as is needed to make the year a qualifying year: the qualifying earnings factor less what they already have, never below nothing.
@export How much of a credit am I given for this year, in pounds (reg 25(2))?
GIVEN `the credit I would otherwise be given` IS A NUMBER @desc What credit, in pounds, would you otherwise be given for the year or the week?
      `the earnings factors I already have for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What earnings factors, in pounds, do you already have for the year?
      `the qualifying earnings factor for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the qualifying earnings factor for the year, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of a credit am I given for this year, in pounds` IS
    `regulation 25(2): the amount the person is credited with` `the credit I would otherwise be given` `the earnings factors I already have for the year` `the qualifying earnings factor for the year`


§§§ `Years before 6 April 2016 (regs 26 to 28)`

-- Reg 26. What the person would have been entitled to under the Social Security (Credits) Regulations 1975 for a Category A retirement pension, had the 2014 Act amendment not come into force and the person reached pensionable age on 6 April 2016.
-- That amount is supplied (the 1975 Regulations are not an input). NOTHING for a week in Chapter 3.
@export What am I credited with for a year before 6 April 2016 under the 1975 Credits Regulations, in pounds (reg 26)?
GIVEN `the first day of the week I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the week you are asking about?
      `what I would have been entitled to under the 1975 Regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc What would you have been entitled to be credited with under the 1975 Credits Regulations, on those assumptions, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What am I credited with for a year before 6 April 2016 under the 1975 Credits Regulations, in pounds` IS
    `regulation 26: the earnings or contributions credited under the 1975 Regulations` `the first day of the week I am asking about` `what I would have been entitled to under the 1975 Regulations`

-- Reg 27. What the person would have been entitled to under section 23A of the 1992 Act on the same assumptions. NOTHING for a week in Chapter 3.
@export What Class 3 contribution am I credited with as a parent or carer for a year before 6 April 2016, in pounds (reg 27)?
GIVEN `the first day of the week I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the week you are asking about?
      `what I would have been entitled to under section 23A` IS A NUMBER @desc What Class 3 contribution would you have been entitled to under section 23A of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992, on those assumptions, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What Class 3 contribution am I credited with as a parent or carer for a year before 6 April 2016, in pounds` IS
    `regulation 27: the Class 3 contribution credited for parents and carers` `the first day of the week I am asking about` `what I would have been entitled to under section 23A`

-- Regs 28 and 33 are word for word the same except paragraph (3): 28 is for a tax year beginning on or after 6 April 1975 and ending before 6 April 2016, 33 for one beginning on or after 6 April 2016
-- (checked by diffing the source lines, NOTES.md finding 15). The Chapter of reg 25(1) picks which. Requires the member's earnings factors to exceed the qualifying earnings factor, an application for a past period, and no other entitlement.
@export Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution for this week as the spouse or civil partner of a member of the forces (regs 28, 33)?
GIVEN `the first day of the week I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the week you are asking about?
      `I am a spouse or civil partner of a member of the forces, or treated as one for accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a spouse or civil partner of a member of Her Majesty's forces, or treated by the Secretary of State as one for the purposes of occupying accommodation?
      `I am accompanying the member on an assignment outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you accompanying the member of the forces on an assignment outside the United Kingdom (or treated by the Secretary of State as doing so)?
      `the member's earnings factors for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the member's earnings factors for the year, in pounds?
      `the qualifying earnings factor for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the qualifying earnings factor for the year, in pounds?
      `I am entitled to be credited with earnings for the week under the 1975 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to be credited with earnings for that week under regulation 7A, 8A, 8B or 9E of the 1975 Credits Regulations?
      `I am a woman with a reduced rate election in force for part of the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a woman who has a reduced rate election (the married woman's option under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act) in force for any part of the week?
      `I have applied to be credited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State received your application to be credited?
      `my application is for a past period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application for a past period?
      `my application is on an approved form or in a manner accepted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application on a form approved by the Secretary of State, or made in a way the Secretary of State accepts as sufficient?
      `my application includes the information specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your application include the information specified by the Secretary of State or HM Revenue and Customs?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution for this week as the spouse or civil partner of a member of the forces` IF
    CONSIDER `regulation 25(1): the Chapter that makes provision for the week` `the first day of the week I am asking about`
    WHEN `Chapter 2 (a pre-commencement qualifying year)` THEN `regulation 28(1): the person is credited with a Class 3 contribution for the week` `my forces spouse facts`
    WHEN `Chapter 3 (a qualifying year or a post-commencement qualifying year)` THEN `regulation 33(1): the person is credited with a Class 3 contribution for the week` `my forces spouse facts`
    WHERE
        `my forces spouse facts` MEANS ForcesSpouseFacts WITH
            `the first day of the week` IS `the first day of the week I am asking about`
            `the person is a spouse or civil partner of a member of Her Majesty's forces, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State for the purposes of occupying accommodation` IS `I am a spouse or civil partner of a member of the forces, or treated as one for accommodation`
            `the person is accompanying the member of Her Majesty's forces on an assignment outside the United Kingdom, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State` IS `I am accompanying the member on an assignment outside the United Kingdom`
            `the earnings factors of the member of Her Majesty's forces for the year` IS `the member's earnings factors for the year`
            `the qualifying earnings factor for the year` IS `the qualifying earnings factor for the year`
            `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings for the week under regulation 7A, 8A, 8B or 9E of the 1975 Regulations` IS `I am entitled to be credited with earnings for the week under the 1975 Regulations`
            `the person is a woman for whom an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force for any part of the week` IS `I am a woman with a reduced rate election in force for part of the week`
            `an application to be credited has been received by the Secretary of State` IS `I have applied to be credited`
            `the application is made in respect of a past period` IS `my application is for a past period`
            `the application is on a form approved by the Secretary of State, or made in a manner the Secretary of State accepts as sufficient` IS `my application is on an approved form or in a manner accepted`
            `the application includes the information specified by the Secretary of State or the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs` IS `my application includes the information specified`

-- Reg 28(5), (6) (and 33). The person's side: an application received for a past period, on an approved form or in a manner the Secretary of State accepts, with the information specified.
@export Does my application to be credited as the spouse or civil partner of a member of the forces contain what the Regulations require (reg 28(5), (6))?
GIVEN `I have applied to be credited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State received your application to be credited?
      `my application is for a past period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application for a past period?
      `my application is on an approved form or in a manner accepted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application on a form approved by the Secretary of State, or made in a way the Secretary of State accepts as sufficient?
      `my application includes the information specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your application include the information specified by the Secretary of State or HM Revenue and Customs?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my application to be credited as the spouse or civil partner of a member of the forces contain what the Regulations require` IF
    `regulation 28(5) and (6): a valid application has been received` `my forces spouse facts`
    WHERE
        `my forces spouse facts` MEANS ForcesSpouseFacts WITH
            -- Placeholders: the rule called reads only the four application fields.
            `the first day of the week` IS (YMD 2010 6 7)
            `the person is a spouse or civil partner of a member of Her Majesty's forces, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State for the purposes of occupying accommodation` IS TRUE
            `the person is accompanying the member of Her Majesty's forces on an assignment outside the United Kingdom, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State` IS TRUE
            `the earnings factors of the member of Her Majesty's forces for the year` IS 0
            `the qualifying earnings factor for the year` IS 0
            `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings for the week under regulation 7A, 8A, 8B or 9E of the 1975 Regulations` IS FALSE
            `the person is a woman for whom an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force for any part of the week` IS FALSE
            `an application to be credited has been received by the Secretary of State` IS `I have applied to be credited`
            `the application is made in respect of a past period` IS `my application is for a past period`
            `the application is on a form approved by the Secretary of State, or made in a manner the Secretary of State accepts as sufficient` IS `my application is on an approved form or in a manner accepted`
            `the application includes the information specified by the Secretary of State or the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs` IS `my application includes the information specified`


§§§ `Credits for benefits, tax credits and age (regs 29 to 33)`

-- Reg 29. A credit under one of nine listed provisions of the 1975 Regulations (approved training, carer's allowance, disability element of working tax credit, unemployment, incapacity, jury service, maternity pay, imprisonment, forces spouses) also counts for the 2014 Act.
@export Is a credit I get under the 1975 Credits Regulations also given for my State Pension (reg 29)?
GIVEN `the provision I am credited under` IS A ProvisionOfThe1975Regulations @desc Which provision of the 1975 Credits Regulations are you credited under?
      `I am credited with earnings or contributions under it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you credited with earnings or contributions under it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a credit I get under the 1975 Credits Regulations also given for my State Pension` IF
    `regulation 29(1): the person is also credited for the purposes of Part 1 of the 2014 Act` `the provision I am credited under` `I am credited with earnings or contributions under it`

-- Reg 30. Working tax credit paid for the week to an employed earner, a low-profit self-employed earner or a person excepted by reg 43; for a couple, to the member assessed (or, if both are, the member paid); not if credited under 7B, 8A or 8B, nor for a woman
-- with a reduced rate election. The words '... would otherwise ... be treated' of (1)(b) are as the converter text has them (fork F30).
@export Am I credited with earnings for this week because I am paid working tax credit (reg 30)?
GIVEN `I am paid working tax credit for the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is working tax credit paid to you in respect of the week?
      `the kind of worker I am in the week` IS A KindOfEarner @desc In that week, which are you: an employed earner; a self-employed earner whose profits are below the small profits threshold; a person excepted by regulation 43 of the Social Security (Contributions) Regulations 2001; or another kind of person?
      `working tax credit is paid for me and my partner as a couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is working tax credit paid in respect of you and your partner as a couple?
      `only one of us is assessed as having earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are a couple: is only one of you assessed as having income consisting of earnings?
      `I am the one assessed as having earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, are you the member assessed as having earnings?
      `working tax credit is paid to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If both are assessed, is working tax credit paid to you?
      `I am entitled to be credited with earnings for the week under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to be credited with earnings for the week under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B of the 1975 Credits Regulations?
      `I am a woman with a reduced rate election in force for part of the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a woman who has a reduced rate election in force for any part of the week?
      `the lower earnings limit for the week` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lower earnings limit in force for the week, in pounds?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I credited with earnings for this week because I am paid working tax credit` IF
    `regulation 30: the person is credited with earnings for the week` `my tax credit facts`
    WHERE
        `my tax credit facts` MEANS WorkingTaxCreditFacts WITH
            `working tax credit is paid in respect of the week` IS `I am paid working tax credit for the week`
            `the kind of person the person is in the week` IS `the kind of worker I am in the week`
            `working tax credit is paid in respect of a couple` IS `working tax credit is paid for me and my partner as a couple`
            `only one member of the couple is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS `only one of us is assessed as having earnings`
            `the person is the member of the couple who is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS `I am the one assessed as having earnings`
            `the person is the member of the couple to whom working tax credit is paid` IS `working tax credit is paid to me`
            `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings for the week under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B of the 1975 Regulations` IS `I am entitled to be credited with earnings for the week under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B`
            `the person is a woman for whom an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force for any part of the week` IS `I am a woman with a reduced rate election in force for part of the week`
            `the lower earnings limit then in force in respect of the week` IS `the lower earnings limit for the week`

-- Reg 30(1). Earnings equal to the lower earnings limit then in force in respect of the week. NOTHING where reg 30 does not credit the person.
@export How much earnings am I credited with for a week in which I am paid working tax credit, in pounds (reg 30(1))?
GIVEN `I am paid working tax credit for the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is working tax credit paid to you in respect of the week?
      `the kind of worker I am in the week` IS A KindOfEarner @desc In that week, which are you: an employed earner; a self-employed earner whose profits are below the small profits threshold; a person excepted by regulation 43 of the Social Security (Contributions) Regulations 2001; or another kind of person?
      `working tax credit is paid for me and my partner as a couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is working tax credit paid in respect of you and your partner as a couple?
      `only one of us is assessed as having earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are a couple: is only one of you assessed as having income consisting of earnings?
      `I am the one assessed as having earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, are you the member assessed as having earnings?
      `working tax credit is paid to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If both are assessed, is working tax credit paid to you?
      `I am entitled to be credited with earnings for the week under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to be credited with earnings for the week under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B of the 1975 Credits Regulations?
      `I am a woman with a reduced rate election in force for part of the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a woman who has a reduced rate election in force for any part of the week?
      `the lower earnings limit for the week` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lower earnings limit in force for the week, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much earnings am I credited with for a week in which I am paid working tax credit, in pounds` IS
    `regulation 30(1): the earnings credited` `my tax credit facts`
    WHERE
        `my tax credit facts` MEANS WorkingTaxCreditFacts WITH
            `working tax credit is paid in respect of the week` IS `I am paid working tax credit for the week`
            `the kind of person the person is in the week` IS `the kind of worker I am in the week`
            `working tax credit is paid in respect of a couple` IS `working tax credit is paid for me and my partner as a couple`
            `only one member of the couple is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS `only one of us is assessed as having earnings`
            `the person is the member of the couple who is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS `I am the one assessed as having earnings`
            `the person is the member of the couple to whom working tax credit is paid` IS `working tax credit is paid to me`
            `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings for the week under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B of the 1975 Regulations` IS `I am entitled to be credited with earnings for the week under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B`
            `the person is a woman for whom an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force for any part of the week` IS `I am a woman with a reduced rate election in force for part of the week`
            `the lower earnings limit then in force in respect of the week` IS `the lower earnings limit for the week`

-- Reg 31. A week for any part of which the person is entitled to universal credit under Part 1 of the 2012 Act.
@export Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution for this week because I am entitled to universal credit (reg 31)?
GIVEN `I am entitled to universal credit for some part of the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to universal credit for any part of the week?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution for this week because I am entitled to universal credit` IF
    `regulation 31: the person is credited with a Class 3 contribution for the week` `I am entitled to universal credit for some part of the week`

-- Reg 32. A man born before 6 October 1953, for a week in the tax year he reaches the age that is pensionable age for a woman born the same day, or any later year before the one in which he turns 65;
-- not if he is absent from Great Britain for more than 182 days in the year; a self-employed man only if (a) or (b).
@export Am I credited with earnings for this week as a man approaching State Pension age (reg 32)?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the date I reach the age that is pensionable age for a woman born on my birthday` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you reach the age that is pensionable age for a woman born on the same day as you?
      `the first day of the week I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the week you are asking about?
      `the number of days I am absent from Great Britain during the year` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days in that tax year are you absent from Great Britain?
      `I am a self-employed earner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed earner?
      `I would be treated as having paid a Class 2 contribution but for low profits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If self-employed: would you be treated as having paid a Class 2 contribution, but for the fact that your profits for the year are below the small profits threshold?
      `I am excepted by regulation 43` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If self-employed: are you excepted from being treated as having paid a Class 2 contribution by regulation 43 of the Social Security (Contributions) Regulations 2001, for any week in a year to which regulation 32 applies?
      `the lower earnings limit for the week` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lower earnings limit in force for the week, in pounds?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I credited with earnings for this week as a man approaching State Pension age` IF
    `regulation 32(1): the man is credited with earnings for the week` `my age facts`
    WHERE
        `my age facts` MEANS ApproachingPensionableAgeFacts WITH
            `the man's date of birth` IS `my date of birth`
            `the date the man attains the age which is pensionable age in the case of a woman born on the same day` IS `the date I reach the age that is pensionable age for a woman born on my birthday`
            `the first day of the week` IS `the first day of the week I am asking about`
            `the number of days the man is absent from Great Britain during the year` IS `the number of days I am absent from Great Britain during the year`
            `the man is a self-employed earner` IS `I am a self-employed earner`
            `the man would be treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution but for the fact that his profits for the year are below the small profits threshold specified by section 11(4)(b) of the 1992 Act` IS `I would be treated as having paid a Class 2 contribution but for low profits`
            `the man is excepted from being treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution by virtue of regulation 43 of the Social Security (Contributions) Regulations 2001 in respect of any week in a year to which regulation 32 applies` IS `I am excepted by regulation 43`
            `the lower earnings limit then in force in respect of the week` IS `the lower earnings limit for the week`

-- Reg 32(1). Earnings equal to the lower earnings limit then in force. NOTHING where reg 32 does not credit him.
@export How much earnings am I credited with for that week as a man approaching State Pension age, in pounds (reg 32(1))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the date I reach the age that is pensionable age for a woman born on my birthday` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you reach the age that is pensionable age for a woman born on the same day as you?
      `the first day of the week I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the week you are asking about?
      `the number of days I am absent from Great Britain during the year` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days in that tax year are you absent from Great Britain?
      `I am a self-employed earner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed earner?
      `I would be treated as having paid a Class 2 contribution but for low profits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If self-employed: would you be treated as having paid a Class 2 contribution, but for the fact that your profits for the year are below the small profits threshold?
      `I am excepted by regulation 43` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If self-employed: are you excepted from being treated as having paid a Class 2 contribution by regulation 43 of the Social Security (Contributions) Regulations 2001, for any week in a year to which regulation 32 applies?
      `the lower earnings limit for the week` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lower earnings limit in force for the week, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much earnings am I credited with for that week as a man approaching State Pension age, in pounds` IS
    `regulation 32(1): the earnings credited` `my age facts`
    WHERE
        `my age facts` MEANS ApproachingPensionableAgeFacts WITH
            `the man's date of birth` IS `my date of birth`
            `the date the man attains the age which is pensionable age in the case of a woman born on the same day` IS `the date I reach the age that is pensionable age for a woman born on my birthday`
            `the first day of the week` IS `the first day of the week I am asking about`
            `the number of days the man is absent from Great Britain during the year` IS `the number of days I am absent from Great Britain during the year`
            `the man is a self-employed earner` IS `I am a self-employed earner`
            `the man would be treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution but for the fact that his profits for the year are below the small profits threshold specified by section 11(4)(b) of the 1992 Act` IS `I would be treated as having paid a Class 2 contribution but for low profits`
            `the man is excepted from being treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution by virtue of regulation 43 of the Social Security (Contributions) Regulations 2001 in respect of any week in a year to which regulation 32 applies` IS `I am excepted by regulation 43`
            `the lower earnings limit then in force in respect of the week` IS `the lower earnings limit for the week`


§§§ `Credits for child benefit, caring and fostering (regs 34 to 39)`

-- Reg 34. Either I am awarded child benefit for a child under 12, or I am the partner of the person awarded it, live with them, share responsibility, am ordinarily resident in Great Britain, am not in prison and apply in accordance with reg 39,
-- and their earnings factors (leaving out those derived from child benefit credits) exceed the qualifying earnings factor for the year.
@export Am I entitled to be credited with a Class 3 contribution because child benefit is awarded for a child under 12 (reg 34)?
GIVEN `I am awarded child benefit for part of the week for a child under 12` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you awarded child benefit for any part of the week in respect of a child under 12?
      `I am the partner of the person awarded child benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the partner of a person to whom child benefit is awarded for the week?
      `I live with the person awarded child benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you live with the person to whom child benefit is awarded?
      `I share responsibility for the child with that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you share responsibility for the child with that person?
      `I am ordinarily resident in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you ordinarily resident in Great Britain?
      `I am in prison or legal custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody?
      `I apply to HM Revenue and Customs in accordance with regulation 39` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied to HM Revenue and Customs to be credited, in accordance with regulation 39?
      `all the earnings factors of the person awarded child benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc What are all the earnings factors, in pounds, of the person to whom child benefit is awarded, for the year?
      `of those, the part derived from credits for being awarded child benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that, in pounds, comes from contributions credited because they were awarded child benefit?
      `the qualifying earnings factor for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the qualifying earnings factor for the year, in pounds?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to be credited with a Class 3 contribution because child benefit is awarded for a child under 12` IF
    `regulation 34(1): the person is entitled to be credited with a Class 3 contribution for the week` `my child benefit facts`
    WHERE
        `my child benefit facts` MEANS ChildBenefitCreditFacts WITH
            `the person is awarded child benefit for any part of the week in respect of a child under the age of 12` IS `I am awarded child benefit for part of the week for a child under 12`
            `the person is the partner of a person to whom child benefit is awarded for the week` IS `I am the partner of the person awarded child benefit`
            `the person resides with the person to whom child benefit is awarded` IS `I live with the person awarded child benefit`
            `the person shares responsibility with that person for the child in respect of whom child benefit is awarded` IS `I share responsibility for the child with that person`
            `the person is ordinarily resident in Great Britain` IS `I am ordinarily resident in Great Britain`
            `the person is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody` IS `I am in prison or legal custody`
            `the person makes an application to the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs to be so credited in accordance with regulation 39` IS `I apply to HM Revenue and Customs in accordance with regulation 39`
            `all the earnings factors of the person to whom child benefit is awarded for the year` IS `all the earnings factors of the person awarded child benefit`
            `of those, the earnings factors derived from contributions credited by virtue of that person being awarded child benefit` IS `of those, the part derived from credits for being awarded child benefit`
            `the qualifying earnings factor for the year` IS `the qualifying earnings factor for the year`

-- Reg 35. I provided care for a child under 12 and am one of the listed relatives, was ordinarily resident in Great Britain, child benefit was awarded to someone else for the child and the week, their earnings factors exceed the qualifying earnings factor, and I applied.
-- Where several people could satisfy the care condition, only the person they elect (with the agreement of the person awarded child benefit), or failing agreement the Secretary of State chooses, is credited (fork F35).
@export Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution for this week because I cared for a child under 12 (reg 35(1) to (4))?
GIVEN `I provided care in the week for a child under 12` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you provide care in the week for a child under 12?
      `my relationship to the child` IS A CarerRelationship @desc How are you related to the child (see the Regulations' list: non-resident parent, grandparent, great-grandparent, great-great-grandparent, sibling, a parent's sibling, their spouse, civil partner or partner, or a son or daughter of those)?
      `I was ordinarily resident in Great Britain in the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you ordinarily resident in Great Britain in the week?
      `child benefit was awarded to another person for the child for that week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was child benefit awarded to another person for the child (or each child) you cared for, and for that week?
      `that person's earnings factors, other than from regulation 34 credits` IS A NUMBER @desc What are that person's earnings factors for the year, in pounds, leaving out any from a Class 3 credit under regulation 34?
      `the qualifying earnings factor for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the qualifying earnings factor for the year, in pounds?
      `I have applied in accordance with paragraph (5) and regulation 39` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied to the Secretary of State in accordance with regulation 35(5) and regulation 39?
      `the number of people who could satisfy the care condition for that week, including me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people, including you, could satisfy the care condition for that week?
      `the carers elected who is to be credited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the carers elected, with the agreement of the person awarded child benefit, which of them is to be credited?
      `the carers elected me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, did they elect you?
      `the Secretary of State has decided who is credited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If they did not agree: has the Secretary of State decided which of them is credited?
      `the Secretary of State decided it is me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, did the Secretary of State decide it is you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution for this week because I cared for a child under 12` IF
    `regulation 35(1): the person is credited with a Class 3 contribution for the week` `my care facts` (`regulation 35(4): which carer is credited` `the number of people who could satisfy the care condition for that week, including me` `the carers elected who is to be credited` `the carers elected me` (IF `the Secretary of State has decided who is credited` THEN JUST `the Secretary of State decided it is me` ELSE NOTHING))
    WHERE
        `my care facts` MEANS ChildCareFacts WITH
            `the person provided care in the week in respect of a child under the age of 12` IS `I provided care in the week for a child under 12`
            `the person's relationship to the child` IS `my relationship to the child`
            `the person was ordinarily resident in Great Britain in the week` IS `I was ordinarily resident in Great Britain in the week`
            `child benefit was awarded to another person, B, in respect of the child (or each child) cared for, and for the week in which the care was provided` IS `child benefit was awarded to another person for the child for that week`
            `B's earnings factors, other than those derived from a Class 3 contribution credit awarded under regulation 34` IS `that person's earnings factors, other than from regulation 34 credits`
            `the qualifying earnings factor for the year in which the week falls` IS `the qualifying earnings factor for the year`
            `the person has made an application to the Secretary of State in accordance with paragraph (5) and regulation 39` IS `I have applied in accordance with paragraph (5) and regulation 39`

-- Reg 35(4). When more than one person can satisfy the care condition, they elect with the agreement of the person awarded child benefit; failing agreement the Secretary of State decides. While neither has happened the text is silent (fork F35).
@export Which of the carers is credited for that week (reg 35(4))?
GIVEN `the number of people who could satisfy the care condition for that week, including me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people, including you, could satisfy the care condition for that week?
      `the carers elected who is to be credited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the carers elected, with the agreement of the person awarded child benefit, which of them is to be credited?
      `the carers elected me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, did they elect you?
      `the Secretary of State has decided who is credited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If they did not agree: has the Secretary of State decided which of them is credited?
      `the Secretary of State decided it is me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, did the Secretary of State decide it is you?
GIVETH A CarerElection
DECIDE `Which of the carers is credited for that week` IS
    `regulation 35(4): which carer is credited` `the number of people who could satisfy the care condition for that week, including me` `the carers elected who is to be credited` `the carers elected me` (IF `the Secretary of State has decided who is credited` THEN JUST `the Secretary of State decided it is me` ELSE NOTHING)

-- Reg 35(6): eleven relationships, (a) to (k); 35(7) and (8) say what a sibling and a partner are.
@export Is my relationship to the child one the Regulations list for a carer's credit (reg 35(6))?
GIVEN `my relationship to the child` IS A CarerRelationship @desc How are you related to the child (see the Regulations' list: non-resident parent, grandparent, great-grandparent, great-great-grandparent, sibling, a parent's sibling, their spouse, civil partner or partner, or a son or daughter of those)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my relationship to the child one the Regulations list for a carer's credit` IF
    `regulation 35(6): the relationship is one the paragraph specifies` `my relationship to the child`

-- Reg 35(7). A sibling includes a half-blood sibling, a step sibling and an adopted sibling.
@export Do I count as a sibling for a carer's credit (reg 35(7))?
GIVEN `I am a sibling of the whole blood` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a sibling of the whole blood?
      `I am a sibling of the half blood` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a sibling of the half blood?
      `I am a step sibling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a step sibling?
      `I am an adopted sibling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an adopted sibling?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I count as a sibling for a carer's credit` IF
    `regulation 35(7): the person counts as a sibling` `I am a sibling of the whole blood` `I am a sibling of the half blood` `I am a step sibling` `I am an adopted sibling`

-- Reg 35(8). The other member of a couple who are not married or civil partners but live together as if they were.
@export Am I a partner for a carer's credit (reg 35(8))?
GIVEN `I am the other member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the other member of a couple?
      `we are married to, or civil partners of, each other` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you married to, or civil partners of, each other?
      `we live together as if we were a married couple or civil partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you live together as if you were a married couple or civil partners?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a partner for a carer's credit` IF
    `regulation 35(8): the person is a partner` `I am the other member of a couple` `we are married to, or civil partners of, each other` `we live together as if we were a married couple or civil partners`

-- Reg 35(5). The person's side: the name and date of birth of each child; where asked, a declaration by the person awarded child benefit; the week or weeks of care.
@export Does my application for a carer's credit contain what the Regulations require (reg 35(5))?
GIVEN `my application includes the name and date of birth of each child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your application include the name and date of birth of the child, or each child, you cared for?
      `a declaration by the person awarded child benefit has been asked for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State or HM Revenue and Customs asked for a declaration by the person awarded child benefit that the conditions are satisfied?
      `my application includes that declaration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your application include that declaration?
      `my application specifies the weeks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your application specify the week or weeks in which each child was cared for?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my application for a carer's credit contain what the Regulations require` IF
    `regulation 35(5): the application has the required content` `my care application`
    WHERE
        `my care application` MEANS ChildCareApplication WITH
            `the application includes the name and date of birth of the child, or each child, cared for` IS `my application includes the name and date of birth of each child`
            `the Secretary of State or the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs have asked for a declaration by B that the conditions in paragraph (2) are satisfied` IS `a declaration by the person awarded child benefit has been asked for`
            `the application includes that declaration by B` IS `my application includes that declaration`
            `the application specifies the relevant week or weeks in which the child, or each child, was cared for` IS `my application specifies the weeks`

-- Reg 36. An approved foster parent (four listed regimes), ordinarily resident in Great Britain, not in prison, who applies to HM Revenue and Customs in accordance with reg 39.
@export Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution for this week because I am a foster parent (reg 36)?
GIVEN `how I am approved` IS A FosterApproval @desc How are you approved: as a foster parent in England, a kinship carer or foster carer in Scotland, or a foster parent in Northern Ireland, or not approved in any of those ways?
      `I am ordinarily resident in Great Britain in the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you ordinarily resident in Great Britain in the week?
      `I am in prison or legal custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody?
      `I have applied to HM Revenue and Customs in accordance with regulation 39` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has HM Revenue and Customs received your application to be credited, in accordance with regulation 39?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution for this week because I am a foster parent` IF
    `regulation 36: the person is credited with a Class 3 contribution for the week` `my fostering facts`
    WHERE
        `my fostering facts` MEANS FosterFacts WITH
            `how the person is approved` IS `how I am approved`
            `the person is ordinarily resident in Great Britain in the week` IS `I am ordinarily resident in Great Britain in the week`
            `the person is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody` IS `I am in prison or legal custody`
            `an application to be credited is received by the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs in accordance with regulation 39` IS `I have applied to HM Revenue and Customs in accordance with regulation 39`

-- Reg 36(2). Approved under one of four regimes: England (Fostering Services Regulations 2011), Scotland (kinship carer, or foster carer) or Northern Ireland.
@export Am I a foster parent for the purposes of the credit (reg 36(2))?
GIVEN `how I am approved` IS A FosterApproval @desc How are you approved: as a foster parent in England, a kinship carer or foster carer in Scotland, or a foster parent in Northern Ireland, or not approved in any of those ways?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a foster parent for the purposes of the credit` IF
    `regulation 36(2): the person is a foster parent` `how I am approved`

-- Reg 37. Caring for 20 or more hours in the week for people each entitled to a relevant benefit (or where the Secretary of State considers the level appropriate), or within Schedule 1B to the Income Support Regulations; not while not ordinarily resident in Great Britain or in prison.
-- An application is needed for the hours route except for a woman with a reduced rate election; the Schedule 1B route needs none (fork F36). Caring for no one is not caring for 'each person'.
@export Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution for this week because I am engaged in caring (reg 37)?
GIVEN `the hours I care for others in the week` IS A NUMBER @desc In the week, how many hours in total do you care for another person or persons?
      `each person I care for is entitled to a relevant benefit for the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is each person you care for entitled, for that week, to a relevant benefit (attendance allowance, the middle or highest rate care component of disability living allowance, the daily living component of personal independence payment, or another listed in regulation 37(4))?
      `the Secretary of State considers that level of care appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Secretary of State consider that level of care appropriate?
      `paragraph 4, 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B to the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does paragraph 4, 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B to the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987 apply to you?
      `I am not ordinarily resident in Great Britain for the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not ordinarily resident in Great Britain for the period?
      `I am in prison or legal custody for the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody for the period?
      `I am a woman with a reduced rate election in force for part of the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a woman who has a reduced rate election in force for any part of the week?
      `I have applied in accordance with paragraph (6) and regulation 39` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State received your application to be credited, in accordance with regulation 37(6) and regulation 39?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I credited with a Class 3 contribution for this week because I am engaged in caring` IF
    `regulation 37(1): the person is credited with a Class 3 contribution for the week` `my caring facts`
    WHERE
        `my caring facts` MEANS CaringFacts WITH
            `the total number of hours the person cares for another person or persons in the week` IS `the hours I care for others in the week`
            `the Secretary of State considers that level of care appropriate` IS `the Secretary of State considers that level of care appropriate`
            `paragraph 4, 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B to the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987 applies to the person` IS `paragraph 4, 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B to the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987 applies to me`
            `the person is not ordinarily resident in Great Britain for the period` IS `I am not ordinarily resident in Great Britain for the period`
            `the person is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody for the period` IS `I am in prison or legal custody for the period`
            `the person is a woman for whom an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force for any part of the week` IS `I am a woman with a reduced rate election in force for part of the week`
            `an application to be credited is received by the Secretary of State in accordance with paragraph (6) and regulation 39` IS `I have applied in accordance with paragraph (6) and regulation 39`
            -- Only whether each person cared for is on a relevant benefit matters to regulation 37(2)(a)(i), so a placeholder benefit stands for the answer.
            `the benefit each person cared for is entitled to for the week` IS IF `each person I care for is entitled to a relevant benefit for the week` THEN LIST `attendance allowance in accordance with section 64 of the 1992 Act` ELSE LIST `no benefit that regulation 37(4) lists`

-- Reg 37(2), (3): the hours route or Schedule 1B, and not while not ordinarily resident in Great Britain or in prison. No application is considered.
@export Am I engaged in caring in the week for the Regulations' purposes (reg 37(2))?
GIVEN `the hours I care for others in the week` IS A NUMBER @desc In the week, how many hours in total do you care for another person or persons?
      `each person I care for is entitled to a relevant benefit for the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is each person you care for entitled, for that week, to a relevant benefit (attendance allowance, the middle or highest rate care component of disability living allowance, the daily living component of personal independence payment, or another listed in regulation 37(4))?
      `the Secretary of State considers that level of care appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Secretary of State consider that level of care appropriate?
      `paragraph 4, 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B to the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does paragraph 4, 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B to the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987 apply to you?
      `I am not ordinarily resident in Great Britain for the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not ordinarily resident in Great Britain for the period?
      `I am in prison or legal custody for the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody for the period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I engaged in caring in the week for the Regulations' purposes` IF
    `regulation 37(2): the person is engaged in caring in the week` `my caring facts`
    WHERE
        `my caring facts` MEANS CaringFacts WITH
            `the total number of hours the person cares for another person or persons in the week` IS `the hours I care for others in the week`
            `the Secretary of State considers that level of care appropriate` IS `the Secretary of State considers that level of care appropriate`
            `paragraph 4, 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B to the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987 applies to the person` IS `paragraph 4, 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B to the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987 applies to me`
            `the person is not ordinarily resident in Great Britain for the period` IS `I am not ordinarily resident in Great Britain for the period`
            `the person is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody for the period` IS `I am in prison or legal custody for the period`
            -- Placeholders: regulation 37(2) reads neither the election nor the application.
            `the person is a woman for whom an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force for any part of the week` IS FALSE
            `an application to be credited is received by the Secretary of State in accordance with paragraph (6) and regulation 39` IS FALSE
            `the benefit each person cared for is entitled to for the week` IS IF `each person I care for is entitled to a relevant benefit for the week` THEN LIST `attendance allowance in accordance with section 64 of the 1992 Act` ELSE LIST `no benefit that regulation 37(4) lists`

-- Reg 37(4): attendance allowance, pension age disability payment, the middle or highest rate care component of disability living allowance, an increase of disablement pension, a 100% disablement benefit, constant attendance allowance, the daily living component of personal independence payment, armed forces independence payment, and the Scottish child, adult and adult-DLA payments.
@export Is the benefit the person I care for gets a relevant benefit (reg 37(4))?
GIVEN `the benefit the person I care for gets` IS A BenefitOfPersonCaredFor @desc Which of the benefits listed in regulation 37(4) does the person you care for get? (Choose the last if none.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the benefit the person I care for gets a relevant benefit` IF
    `regulation 37(4): the benefit is a relevant benefit` `the benefit the person I care for gets`

-- Reg 37(6). The person's side: a declaration of 20 hours or more; each person's name and (where known) national insurance number; where applicable which relevant benefit each is entitled to; where requested, a signed declaration of the level of care.
@export Does my application for a carer's credit contain what the Regulations require (reg 37(6))?
GIVEN `my application includes my declaration of 20 hours or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your application include your declaration that you care for a person or persons for 20 or more hours in a week?
      `my application includes the name and national insurance number of each person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your application include the name and, where known, the national insurance number of each person you care for?
      `a person I care for is entitled to a relevant benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a person you care for entitled to a relevant benefit?
      `my application says which relevant benefit each person gets` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your application say which relevant benefit each person gets?
      `the Secretary of State has asked for a declaration of the level of care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State asked for a declaration as to the level of care required?
      `my application includes that declaration signed by an appropriate person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your application include a declaration, signed by an appropriate person, of the level of care each person needs?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my application for a carer's credit contain what the Regulations require` IF
    `regulation 37(6): the application has the required content` `my caring application`
    WHERE
        `my caring application` MEANS CaringApplication WITH
            `the application includes a declaration by the applicant that the applicant cares for a person or persons for 20 or more hours in a week` IS `my application includes my declaration of 20 hours or more`
            `the application includes the name and, where known, the national insurance number of each person cared for` IS `my application includes the name and national insurance number of each person`
            `a person cared for is entitled to a relevant benefit` IS `a person I care for is entitled to a relevant benefit`
            `the application says which relevant benefit each person cared for is entitled to` IS `my application says which relevant benefit each person gets`
            `the Secretary of State has asked for a declaration as to the level of care required` IS `the Secretary of State has asked for a declaration of the level of care`
            `the application includes a declaration signed by an appropriate person as to the level of care required for each person cared for` IS `my application includes that declaration signed by an appropriate person`

-- Reg 37(7). Involved in the health care or social care of the person cared for, and considered by the Secretary of State appropriate to make the declaration.
@export Is the person who signs my level-of-care declaration an appropriate person (reg 37(7))?
GIVEN `they are involved in the health care or social care of the person I care for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the signer involved in the health care or social care of the person you care for?
      `the Secretary of State considers them appropriate to make the declaration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Secretary of State consider them appropriate to make a declaration of the level of care required?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the person who signs my level-of-care declaration an appropriate person` IF
    `regulation 37(7): the person is an appropriate person` `they are involved in the health care or social care of the person I care for` `the Secretary of State considers them appropriate to make the declaration`

-- Reg 38(1). Twelve weeks (84 days, fork F33) before the date of entitlement, or after the end of the week in which entitlement or the caring condition ceases.
@export On what day does my extra 12 weeks of credit for caring begin (reg 38(1))?
GIVEN `when the extra credit runs` IS A AdditionalPeriodKind @desc Is the extra credit for the 12 weeks before you become entitled to carer's allowance or the carer support payment component, the 12 weeks after you cease to be entitled, or the 12 weeks after you stop satisfying regulation 37(2)(a)?
      `the date I became entitled, or the last day of the week I ceased` IS A DATE @desc What date: the date you become entitled to carer's allowance or carer support payment (for the first kind), or the last day of the week in which you cease to be entitled or stop satisfying regulation 37(2)(a) (for the others)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day does my extra 12 weeks of credit for caring begin` IS
    (`regulation 38(1): the period of 12 weeks` `when the extra credit runs` `the date I became entitled, or the last day of the week I ceased`)'s `first day of the period`

-- Reg 38(1). The last of the 84 days.
@export On what day does my extra 12 weeks of credit for caring end (reg 38(1))?
GIVEN `when the extra credit runs` IS A AdditionalPeriodKind @desc Is the extra credit for the 12 weeks before you become entitled to carer's allowance or the carer support payment component, the 12 weeks after you cease to be entitled, or the 12 weeks after you stop satisfying regulation 37(2)(a)?
      `the date I became entitled, or the last day of the week I ceased` IS A DATE @desc What date: the date you become entitled to carer's allowance or carer support payment (for the first kind), or the last day of the week in which you cease to be entitled or stop satisfying regulation 37(2)(a) (for the others)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day does my extra 12 weeks of credit for caring end` IS
    (`regulation 38(1): the period of 12 weeks` `when the extra credit runs` `the date I became entitled, or the last day of the week I ceased`)'s `last day of the period`

-- Reg 38(1), (2). The day is in the period unless, for the after-entitlement kind, the person is entitled that week to be credited under regulation 7A of the 1975 Regulations.
@export Is this day within my extra 12 weeks of credit for caring (reg 38(1), (2))?
GIVEN `when the extra credit runs` IS A AdditionalPeriodKind @desc Is the extra credit for the 12 weeks before you become entitled to carer's allowance or the carer support payment component, the 12 weeks after you cease to be entitled, or the 12 weeks after you stop satisfying regulation 37(2)(a)?
      `the date I became entitled, or the last day of the week I ceased` IS A DATE @desc What date: the date you become entitled to carer's allowance or carer support payment (for the first kind), or the last day of the week in which you cease to be entitled or stop satisfying regulation 37(2)(a) (for the others)?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
      `I am entitled that week to a credit under regulation 7A of the 1975 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For that week, are you entitled to be credited under regulation 7A of the 1975 Regulations, by virtue of an allowance under section 70 of the 1992 Act or the carer support payment component of carer support?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this day within my extra 12 weeks of credit for caring` IF
    `regulation 38: the day is credited` `when the extra credit runs` `the date I became entitled, or the last day of the week I ceased` `the day I am asking about` (`regulation 38(2): the week is excluded from the credit` `when the extra credit runs` `I am entitled that week to a credit under regulation 7A of the 1975 Regulations`)

-- Reg 39. The person's duty. For regs 34(1)(b), 36 and 37: before the end of the tax year after the one in which the week falls (the last day counts, fork F32), or within such further time as is allowed (fork F34).
-- For reg 35, as written: AFTER the end of the year in which the week falls, with no latest date (fork F31).
@export Is my application for a credit received in time (reg 39)?
GIVEN `the kind of application I make` IS A KindOfApplication @desc Is it an application under regulation 34(1)(b), 36 or 37, or an application under regulation 35?
      `the first day of a week my application is about` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of a week your application is about?
      `the date my application is received` IS A DATE @desc On what date is your application received?
      `the Secretary of State or HM Revenue and Customs allowed a further time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Secretary of State or HM Revenue and Customs allow you a further time that they consider reasonable in the circumstances?
      `the last day of that further time` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the last day of that further time? (Give any date if none.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my application for a credit received in time` IF
    `regulation 39: the application is received in time` `my application timing`
    WHERE
        `my application timing` MEANS ApplicationTimeFacts WITH
            `the kind of application` IS `the kind of application I make`
            `the first day of a week which is the subject of the application` IS `the first day of a week my application is about`
            `the date the application is received` IS `the date my application is received`
            `the last day of any further time that the Secretary of State or the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs consider reasonable in the circumstances` IS IF `the Secretary of State or HM Revenue and Customs allowed a further time` THEN JUST `the last day of that further time` ELSE NOTHING

